// Generated by scripts/build-requirements.py from the requirements specification. Do not edit by hand.
export default {
 "intro": "<p>Functional requirements are grouped by capability, in the order a client's matter moves through the ministry. Each one lists the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#obligation\">policy obligations</a> it meets (<strong>Obligations</strong>) and the architecture parameters that test it (<strong>Parameters</strong>). Where a requirement has no obligation, its authority is the architecture section named in its rationale. Appendix E and the companion file <code>ARC-001-REQ-v1.0-traceability.csv</code> map all 270 obligations to requirements.</p><p><strong>Module</strong> names the delivery module in which the requirement must first be met (<a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#target-architecture\">target architecture</a> §A.8). Requirements assigned to <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#module\">M0</a> are foundations. Several of them cannot be added later, once the first event, copy, rule or <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#client-group\">cohort</a> exists (PRIN §V) <span class=\"cite\">PRIN-C5</span>.</p>",
 "groups": [
  {
   "id": "a-decisions-and-the-decision-record",
   "title": "A. Decisions and the decision record",
   "intro": "",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "FR-001",
     "anchor": "fr-001",
     "title": "Decision types and what the decision record holds",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 0,
     "moduleText": "M0 (schema), M5 (first rule surface)",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "The system records every decision as one of three types:",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system records every decision as one of three types: grant; deny; or reduce or discontinue. Each is a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#determination\">determination</a> in its own right. Its record states the criteria met and not met, the statutory provisions applied, the assumptions made, the evidence lacking, any decision-support report used, and every item of information considered.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-002\">BR-002</a>, UC-1, UC-2</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-D01, OB-D03, OB-D04, OB-D05, OB-D06, OB-D07, OB-D09, OB-D11</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n07\">N07</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n20\">N20</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given any issued determination, when its record is read, then it holds its type, criteria met, criteria not met, provisions applied, assumptions made and evidence lacking as separate fields, none of which can only be recovered by re-running the rules.</li><li>Given a determination informed by a decision-support report, when the record is read, then a full copy of the report is stored with it.</li><li>Given a request to disclose the information considered, when the record is queried, then every item considered can be listed from the record alone.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#watermark\">evidence snapshot</a>, <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#rules-engine\">rules artefact</a>, decision-maker input; <em>Outputs</em>: <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#decision-record\">determination record</a>; <em>Validations</em>: the assumptions and evidence-lacking fields cannot be empty (an explicit \"none\" counts as an answer).</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-008\">FR-008</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-011\">FR-011</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Policy sets out what the record must contain. That includes negative facts, the assumptions made and the evidence lacking, which cannot be rebuilt after the decision (PRIN <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a> amendment (a)).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-002",
     "anchor": "fr-002",
     "title": "Reasons that name the rule applied and the fact behind it",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 5,
     "moduleText": "M5",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Every decision carries real reasons, generated from the decision trace:",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Every decision carries real reasons, generated from the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#decision-trace\">decision trace</a>: the specific rule, the specific fact, its source and the period it covers. Each rule has its own reasons text, written with the rule and released with it.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-002\">BR-002</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-003\">BR-003</a>, UC-1</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-D02</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n07\">N07</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n18\">N18</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given an adverse determination chosen at random, when its notice is inspected, then each adverse element names the rule identifier, the fact relied on, where that fact came from, and its period.</li><li>Given a rules artefact release, when any rule that produces an adverse outcome lacks approved reasons text, then the release fails.</li><li>Edge case: a category code or a generic \"you do not meet the criteria\" paragraph is not accepted as reasons.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: decision trace; reasons text keyed by rule identifier; <em>Outputs</em>: reasons text bound into the notice; <em>Validations</em>: every adverse rule that fired has reasons text.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-062\">FR-062</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-090\">FR-090</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>A person cannot challenge reasons they cannot trace to a rule and a fact. Untraceable reasons were a defining feature of the automated-debt failure the architecture designs against (TA §C.8.7).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-003",
     "anchor": "fr-003",
     "title": "Decision classes and the human decision-maker",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 0,
     "moduleText": "M0 (schema), M5",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Every output of a rules artefact carries a decision class.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Every output of a rules artefact carries a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#decision-class\">decision class</a>. The policy author declares it, the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#program-policy-authority\">program policy authority</a> approves it on legal advice, and the system enforces it when running. There are three classes:</p><ul><li>an administrative decision, which needs reasons and a route to challenge it;</li><li>a decision that needs a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#human-dm\">human decision-maker</a> before it issues, held until that person records it;</li><li>a computational intermediate, which is never presented as a decision.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-002\">BR-002</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-005\">BR-005</a>, UC-1, UC-7</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n07\">N07</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a rules artefact with an unclassified output, when release is attempted, then release is refused.</li><li>Given a determination whose adverse outcome rests on any inferred, estimated, averaged or apportioned input, when it is computed, then it is held for a human decision-maker, whatever class the artefact declares <span class=\"cite\">TA-C14</span>.</li><li>Given a held determination, when no human decision is recorded, then nothing issues and no timeout issues it automatically.</li><li>Given a computational intermediate, when any client-facing screen or notice would present it as a decision, then the output is blocked and a governance defect is raised.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: class on the artefact; where each input came from; <em>Outputs</em>: class recorded on the determination; <code>DiscretionaryDetermination</code> evidence for human decisions; <em>Validations</em>: a human decision records identity, authority and rationale.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-093\">FR-093</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>The duty to give reasons attaches to the decision, not to the software, and operating procedures break down at volume (TA §B.4.4, §D.5). <strong>Open item</strong>: the architecture names the classes three ways, with different ordering: (i)/(ii)/(iii) at §B.4.4, Class 1/2/3 at §C.8.5 and Class A/B/C at §D.5. This document uses the §D.5 A/B/C names. The Chief Architect is asked to adopt one set throughout.</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-004",
     "anchor": "fr-004",
     "title": "Who may decide, value bands, and reasoning that cannot be handed off",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 4,
     "moduleText": "M4 (routing), M5",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "The system routes each decision to the person or body with authority for it, by entitlement and, where policy sets one, by value band.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system routes each decision to the person or body with authority for it, by entitlement and, where policy sets one, by value band. It records the person who reasoned the decision as the decision-maker of record. It keeps anything the system or another person proposed separate from what the decision-maker concluded.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-002\">BR-002</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-003\">BR-003</a>, UC-1, UC-3</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-D10, OB-EL-23, OB-EL-74, OB-SU-02, OB-SU-32, OB-SU-62, OB-SU-63</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a decision whose value or type needs a higher authority, when a worker without that authority tries to finalise it, then the system routes it to the required authority and refuses to finalise it.</li><li>Given any decision where a recommendation or pre-filled outcome was shown, when the record is read, then the proposal and the decision-maker's conclusion are recorded separately <span class=\"cite\">PRIN-C6</span>.</li><li>Given a request to close or re-open a type of case that needs a named approver, when no approval is recorded, then the action is refused.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: the schedule of delegated authority (reference data with effective dates); <em>Outputs</em>: decision-maker identity and authority on the record; <em>Validations</em>: the authority was in force on the decision date.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-094\">FR-094</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Policy says a decision-maker \"must not delegate the actual decision or allow advice to take the place of their own reasoning\". It also sets decision-makers by dollar band, up to Executive Director and ADM (PRIN <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a>).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-005",
     "anchor": "fr-005",
     "title": "Effective dates worked out by rule, for each part of the benefit",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 5,
     "moduleText": "M5",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "A versioned rule works out the effective date of every determination, including one that replaces an earlier determination, a reconsideration outcome, and a re-determination after the tribunal rescinds a decision.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>A versioned rule works out the effective date of every determination, including one that replaces an earlier determination, a reconsideration outcome, and a re-determination after the tribunal rescinds a decision. The date is worked out separately for each <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#benefit-component\">benefit component</a> and recorded as derived. The ministry's own timeliness is one of the inputs.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-003\">BR-003</a>, UC-2, UC-4</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-R11, OB-A08, OB-SU-79</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a determination granting several components, when it is recorded, then each component carries its own effective date and the version of the rule that worked it out.</li><li>Given a decision issued after its legal time limit expired, when the effective date is worked out, then the earlier date the clock rule sets is applied automatically, without anyone asking.</li><li>Given two components policy does not allow in the same month, when both would otherwise be granted, then the determination grants only what the rule allows and records why.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: benefit type, component, clock state; <em>Outputs</em>: effective dates per component, marked as derived; <em>Validations</em>: no effective date entered by hand without a recorded override authority.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-061\">FR-061</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-090\">FR-090</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>A determination that replaces an earlier one does not take effect on the day it is made. Policy sets the date by benefit type. Where the ministry decided late, policy sets it as the date the decision was due (PRIN <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a> amendment v3.1).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-006",
     "anchor": "fr-006",
     "title": "A pre-decision letter, kept separate from a decision",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 5,
     "moduleText": "M5",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "The system supports a pre-decision communication as its own kind of record, separate from a determination and available to any part of the system that makes decisions.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system supports a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#pre-decision\">pre-decision communication</a> as its own kind of record, separate from a determination and available to any part of the system that makes decisions. It carries reasons, a response deadline, what happens if the client responds or does not, and a plain statement that no decision has been made yet.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-003\">BR-003</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-005\">BR-005</a>, UC-1, UC-5</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-EL-27</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a pre-decision communication, when its notice is generated, then it states the issues, the response due date and how to respond, and no reconsideration or appeal rights are drawn from it.</li><li>Given a client's response within the window, when it arrives, then it is recorded as evidence for the determination that follows.</li><li>Given a client asks for reconsideration of a pre-decision communication, when the request is made, then it is recorded (<a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-055\">FR-055</a>). The communication's status never causes the request to be refused.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: draft calculation or list of issues, response clock definition; <em>Outputs</em>: pre-decision communication record; <em>Validations</em>: it cannot carry an <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#adjudicability\">adjudicability</a> attribute.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-055\">FR-055</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-061\">FR-061</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>If this were only a status flag on a determination, one rule change could make the system read it as a decision and attach appeal rights to it. The ministry's own intake practice already runs this pattern correctly (NOTE-001 v2.0).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-007",
     "anchor": "fr-007",
     "title": "Checks that must be recorded before an adverse decision",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 5,
     "moduleText": "M5, M8",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Before a sanction, reduction, ineligibility or non-compliance decision, the system requires the checks policy sets out to be recorded as evidence:",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Before a sanction, reduction, ineligibility or non-compliance decision, the system requires the checks policy sets out to be recorded as evidence:</p><ul><li>whether the request made of the client was reasonable;</li><li>the client's ability to meet the obligation;</li><li>any exemption that applies;</li><li>that the requirement was clearly explained and the client had a fair chance to meet it;</li><li>the individual assessment of homelessness risk.</li></ul><p>It prevents a decision based on anticipation or unconfirmed suspicion.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-003\">BR-003</a>, UC-2</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-EL-01, OB-EL-12, OB-EL-24, OB-EL-76, OB-EL-78, OB-IN-49</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n07\">N07</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n20\">N20</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given an adverse decision of a type with registered checks, when any check is unrecorded, then the decision cannot be finalised.</li><li>Given a family unit recorded as homeless or at imminent risk, when a failure to provide information would otherwise make it ineligible, then the rule for that group is applied and the reason recorded.</li><li>Given an ineligibility based on absence, when the qualifying condition has not yet happened, then no ineligibility decision can be recorded.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: registered list of checks per decision type; <em>Outputs</em>: check evidence stored with the determination; <em>Validations</em>: every check answered, including answers recorded as a definite \"no\".</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-011\">FR-011</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>These are policy rules, and each can be checked. Administrative fairness is the principle behind them, not a criterion in its own right <span class=\"cite\">METH-C3</span>.</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-008",
     "anchor": "fr-008",
     "title": "Replay from stored records, and a declared replay horizon",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 0,
     "moduleText": "M0 (declaration), M5",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "Any determination can be replayed from what was stored with it (the rules artefact, the engine version and its archived copy, a full copy of the input snapshot, the decision trace and the notice template) without depending on any running system.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Any determination can be <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#replay\">replayed</a> from what was stored with it (the rules artefact, the engine version and its archived copy, a full copy of the input snapshot, the decision trace and the notice template) without depending on any running system. Before the first live determination, the ministry declares in writing how long replay is guaranteed and what serves as evidence after that.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-002\">BR-002</a>, UC-4</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n07\">N07</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a determination issued in a previous year, when it is replayed in an isolated environment from storage alone, then it produces a decision trace identical to the original, byte for byte.</li><li>Given the archived engine copies inside the declared window, when the scheduled test runs, then every archived copy runs or an alarm is raised.</li><li>Given a determination whose inputs were disposed of, or whose governing policy text was never published, when it is replayed, then the result is marked with the declared limit and points the reader to the trace, the notice and the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#shred-survivor\">shred-survivor set</a>.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: the five stored artefacts; <em>Outputs</em>: replay result with limit markers; <em>Validations</em>: each artefact's digest checks out against the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#hash-chain\">hash chain</a>.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-010\">FR-010</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/quality#nfr-sec-009\">NFR-SEC-009</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>A pointer to a running system is not evidence (PRIN <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a>). The architecture chooses a layered horizon. It keeps a runnable archive for seven years, a written specification with a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#regression-corpus\">regression corpus</a> up to twenty years, and the trace after that <span class=\"cite\">TA-C15</span>. Superseded policy text that was never published shortens that horizon unless it is captured when the rules are loaded <span class=\"cite\">NOTE2-C1</span>.</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-009",
     "anchor": "fr-009",
     "title": "Recording the point in time a decision's facts were read",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 0,
     "moduleText": "M0",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "Every determination records the watermark:",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Every determination records the watermark: the point in the system's history up to which its evidence snapshot was read. The system refuses to issue a determination when the gap between now and the watermark is larger than the limit set for its class.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-002\">BR-002</a>, UC-1, UC-6</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n09\">N09</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given any determination, when its record is read, then the watermark is present.</li><li>Given an interactive determination whose gap is over its limit, when issuance is attempted, then it is refused, the worker sees the reason, and a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#work-item\">work item</a> is raised <span class=\"cite\">TA-C16</span>.</li><li>Given a batch <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#issuance-run\">issuance run</a>, when any contributing data stream is over the batch limit at the start of the run, then the run stops and no partial run issues.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: how far each data stream has been applied; limit per determination class; <em>Outputs</em>: watermark on the record; <em>Validations</em>: limits set from measured lag before the first live determination.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/quality#nfr-p-004\">NFR-P-004</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Two determinations made moments apart can each legitimately see a different set of facts, and without the watermark nothing detects it. This is a required addition to the architecture's parameter set, and in practice it cannot be added later (PRIN <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n09\">N09</a>).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-010",
     "anchor": "fr-010",
     "title": "Several generations of rules running side by side",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 5,
     "moduleText": "M5",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "The system assesses each period against the generation of rules in force for it and keeps every superseded generation runnable.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system assesses each period against the generation of rules in force for it and keeps every superseded generation runnable. Where a transition regulation freezes a set of rules, the system runs that frozen set alongside the live one for as long as the regulation requires.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-010\">BR-010</a>, UC-7</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n07\">N07</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a retroactive recalculation that spans a rule change, when it runs, then each period is assessed against the generation in force for that period and the record names each generation.</li><li>Given a case governed by a frozen transition ruleset, when a determination is made, then the frozen generation is applied and the live generation is not.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#rules-register\">rules register</a> with effective-from and effective-to dates; <em>Outputs</em>: generation identifier per period; <em>Validations</em>: no period assessed against a generation not in force for it.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-090\">FR-090</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-091\">FR-091</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>There is no date on which the whole rule set is current <span class=\"cite\">RULES-C2</span>. <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#cihr\">Child in the Home of a Relative</a> needs a frozen ruleset running alongside the live one indefinitely <span class=\"cite\">OBLG-C6</span>.</p>"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "b-evidence-and-verification",
   "title": "B. Evidence and verification",
   "intro": "",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "FR-011",
     "anchor": "fr-011",
     "title": "The four states of a fact",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 0,
     "moduleText": "M0",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "The fact model tells apart four cases:",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The fact model tells apart four cases: a value never asked for; a question asked and answered \"no\"; evidence that was considered but that policy forbids keeping; and evidence that was disposed of. It enforces the bans on printing, scanning, copying or recording that make some evidence impossible to keep.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-002\">BR-002</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-006\">BR-006</a>, UC-1</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-EL-07, OB-EL-28, OB-EL-29, OB-EL-40, OB-EL-71, OB-EL-72</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n12\">N12</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a capture form, when a question is answered \"no\", then a recorded \"no\" (an <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#asserted-negative\">asserted negative</a>) is stored and can be told apart from a blank.</li><li>Given evidence of a type policy forbids keeping or printing, when a worker tries to print it, scan it to the case or attach it, then the action is refused and the fact is recorded as considered but not kept.</li><li>Given a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#determination\">determination</a> that rests on evidence that could not be kept, when it is recorded, then the record says its <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#replay\">replay</a> chain is incomplete, and why.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: rules on what can be kept, per evidence type; <em>Outputs</em>: fact state on every assertion; <em>Validations</em>: mandatory questions cannot be left blank.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/data#dr-001\">DR-001</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/data#dr-002\">DR-002</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Only a recorded \"no\" can support a determination, and the model must represent \"considered and may not be held\" as a distinct state <span class=\"cite\">PRIN-C7</span>.</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-012",
     "anchor": "fr-012",
     "title": "Corrections, updates, and who made the error",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 0,
     "moduleText": "M0 (schema)",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "Every change to evidence is recorded as either a supersession (the world changed) or a correction (the record was wrong).",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Every change to evidence is recorded as either a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#correction\">supersession</a> (the world changed) or a correction (the record was wrong). Every correction must say whose error it was: the client's, the ministry's, a third party's, or undetermined. Completed declarations are never struck out or overwritten, and both parties sign off on any change to them.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-005\">BR-005</a>, UC-2, UC-5</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-IN-12</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n06\">N06</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a correction submitted without saying whose error it was, when it is submitted, then it is refused.</li><li>Given a change to a completed application, when it is recorded, then the original stays readable and the change carries the attestation of both the client and the worker.</li><li>Given a supersession and a correction affecting the same period, when the overpayment is calculated, then each produces its own separately classified component.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: type of change and whose error; <em>Outputs</em>: correction or supersession event; <em>Validations</em>: whose error is required on every correction.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-051\">FR-051</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>The two kinds of change differ only in how they treat the period a fact was true, and that difference decides whether money can be recovered. The error field must be in the schema before the first event is written (TA §C.7.2).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-013",
     "anchor": "fr-013",
     "title": "Asking for information, and verifying it",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 3,
     "moduleText": "M3, M8",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "When the ministry needs information, the system sends a request that states what is needed, why, the due date, and how to get help or more time.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>When the ministry needs information, the system sends a request that states what is needed, why, the due date, and how to get help or more time. It records contact attempts before any payment is held or changed. It applies the verification rules policy sets for shelter costs, confirmed jobs and other entitlement evidence.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-003\">BR-003</a>, UC-1, UC-2</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-EL-02, OB-EL-26, OB-IN-27, OB-IN-30, OB-IN-43, OB-SU-38, OB-SU-77, OB-SU-78, OB-SU-87</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n02\">N02</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given an information request, when it is issued, then it lists each item required, a due date worked out from its registered clock, and how to get help or an extension.</li><li>Given missing information, when a payment hold or change is proposed, then the system first requires the registered number of recorded contact attempts on the registered channels.</li><li>Given shelter-cost evidence supplied by someone other than the landlord, when it is assessed, then it is not rejected for that reason alone.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: request templates, clock definitions; <em>Outputs</em>: request record, evidence of contact attempts; <em>Validations</em>: due date worked out, never typed.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-061\">FR-061</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-062\">FR-062</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>The client must provide information. The ministry must ask clearly and make reasonable attempts before acting on its absence (OB-EL-02, OB-IN-27, OB-IN-30).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-014",
     "anchor": "fr-014",
     "title": "Monthly reports and reporting changes",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 8,
     "moduleText": "M8",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Recipients report the listed types of change and required earnings each reporting period, on any channel.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Recipients report the listed types of change and required earnings each reporting period, on any channel. Each report identifies its reporting period and has its supporting documents attached. Staff may explain the report but cannot fill it in or change it for the client. An incomplete report starts recorded contact attempts.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-009\">BR-009</a>, UC-2</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-EL-15, OB-EL-16, OB-EL-17, OB-EL-18, OB-EL-19, OB-EL-20, OB-IN-51, OB-SU-22</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n09\">N09</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n15\">N15</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a monthly report, when it is submitted, then each reported change becomes evidence with the period it covers, and each required signature is captured.</li><li>Given a worker session, when the worker tries to enter or change a client's declaration, then the system refuses and offers the assisted-completion route, with the client's attestation, instead.</li><li>Given a report with missing information, when it is processed, then a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#work-item\">work item</a> for the registered contact attempts is raised.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: report, documents; <em>Outputs</em>: <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#fact\">evidence assertions</a>; <em>Validations</em>: every report identifies its reporting period.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-071\">FR-071</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-083\">FR-083</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>The monthly report is the main source of evidence for ongoing entitlement, and policy makes it the client's job (OB-EL-15 to OB-EL-20).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-015",
     "anchor": "fr-015",
     "title": "Third-party checks only with valid consent",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 8,
     "moduleText": "M8",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "The system runs third-party checks only where a valid consent of the right scope and period is on the case.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system runs third-party checks only where a valid consent of the right scope and period is on the case. It runs the mandatory checks at application, eligibility review and compliance review unless a registered deferral applies. It verifies only what the client provided, asking the client first. It attaches every result received, including \"no record found\" results.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-006\">BR-006</a>, UC-1</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-EL-03, OB-EL-04, OB-EL-06, OB-EL-08, OB-EL-09, OB-EL-11, OB-EL-42, OB-IN-53</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n02\">N02</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n13\">N13</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n21\">N21</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a check request, when no valid consent covers its source and period, then the check is refused before any outside call is made.</li><li>Given a verbal consent taken by telephone, when its registered validity runs out without a signature, then checks relying on it are refused.</li><li>Given a mandatory check at a review, when no registered deferral applies, then the review cannot be completed without it.</li><li>Given a check result, when it comes back, then it is recorded as evidence with its source, including \"no record found\" results.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: consent instruments; <em>Outputs</em>: check evidence; <em>Validations</em>: consent scope and period checked at the time of the call.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-075\">FR-075</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-006\">INT-006</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-015\">INT-015</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>A third-party check without valid consent is unlawful collection. Verbal consent is not enough for taxpayer information (OB-EL-06).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-016",
     "anchor": "fr-016",
     "title": "Outstanding arrest warrants",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 8,
     "moduleText": "M8",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "The system treats a warrant as outstanding only when the Ministry of Public Safety and Solicitor General confirms it.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system treats a warrant as outstanding only when the Ministry of Public Safety and Solicitor General confirms it. It refuses warrant enquiries about dependent children or anyone under the registered age. It keeps the warrant alert up to date as warrants are resolved, issues the prescribed letter on confirmation, and applies the shelter entitlement policy sets for the family unit with no manual adjustment.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, UC-1, UC-2</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-EL-36, OB-EL-37, OB-EL-39, OB-EL-41, OB-EL-43</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n07\">N07</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n21\">N21</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a warrant flag without confirmation from the authorised source, when a determination is made, then the flag cannot affect it.</li><li>Given a person under the registered age or a dependent child, when a warrant check is attempted, then it is refused.</li><li>Given a family unit with a confirmed warrant and shelter costs in any band, when shelter is determined, then the amount equals the entitlement policy sets, taken from the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#rules-register\">rules register</a>, with no manual adjustment step.</li><li>Given a resolved warrant, when it is recorded, then the alert updates and the clocks of any dependent supplements respond.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: warrant confirmations (<a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-014\">INT-014</a>); <em>Outputs</em>: warrant evidence, alert; <em>Validations</em>: confirmation source required.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-090\">FR-090</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-014\">INT-014</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Policy states an entitlement the current calculation reaches only through a manual adjustment <span class=\"cite\">OBLG-C1</span>, and the documented workaround itself contains an arithmetic error (RC-05).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-017",
     "anchor": "fr-017",
     "title": "Assets, trusts, registered disability savings plans and structured settlements",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 8,
     "moduleText": "M8",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "The system records:",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system records:</p><ul><li>assets and their verified values;</li><li>the client's evidence where an asset cannot be turned into cash;</li><li>the source of funds for exempt purchases;</li><li>trust and <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#rdsp\">RDSP</a> activity and elections;</li><li>structured-settlement documents.</li></ul><p>Before deciding a case that meets one of the registered trust triggers, the system requires a legal opinion through the ministry's litigation branch. It holds legal opinions as privileged, and it records that eligible clients were told about trust and RDSP exemptions.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-006\">BR-006</a>, UC-1, UC-2</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-EL-44, OB-EL-45, OB-EL-46, OB-EL-47, OB-EL-48, OB-EL-49, OB-EL-50, OB-EL-51, OB-EL-52, OB-EL-53, OB-EL-54, OB-EL-55, OB-EL-56, OB-EL-57, OB-EL-58</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n07\">N07</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n21\">N21</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a case with a registered trust trigger, when no legal opinion is recorded, then the eligibility decision cannot be finalised and the wait shows as a pending item with its own clock.</li><li>Given a legal opinion, when anyone tries to disclose it outside ministry staff without recorded consent from the government's lawyers, then the disclosure is refused.</li><li>Given a worker screen where a trust is discussed, when it is used, then no function offers advice on whether a trust suits the client, or legal or investment advice.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: asset, trust and RDSP evidence; <em>Outputs</em>: asset determinations; <em>Validations</em>: values carry a verification status.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-080\">FR-080</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Asset and trust rules decide eligibility. Several carry legal gates and privilege that the system must enforce rather than leave to memory (OB-EL-51, OB-EL-56).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-018",
     "anchor": "fr-018",
     "title": "Seeking other income, federal benefits and assignments",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 8,
     "moduleText": "M8",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "The system records the client's duty to seek, accept and use all other income, including federal benefits at the ages policy sets.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system records the client's duty to seek, accept and use all other income, including federal benefits at the ages policy sets. It captures the assignments and consents to deduction that policy requires. It notifies a maintenance respondent before the ministry acts on assigned rights. It records confirmations of federal applications and tax filing.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, UC-1, UC-2</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-EL-59, OB-EL-60, OB-EL-61, OB-EL-64, OB-SU-18, OB-SU-19, OB-SU-20, OB-SU-21, OB-SU-64, OB-SU-66, OB-SU-80</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n07\">N07</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n13\">N13</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a client reaching a registered age boundary, when the boundary is crossed, then the federal-benefit obligation that applies and its clock start automatically.</li><li>Given an assignment of maintenance rights, when the ministry is about to act on it, then a notice to the respondent must be recorded first.</li><li>Given an assignment or consent to deduction required at a registered threshold, when it is missing, then the payment that depends on it is held.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: age, income evidence, assignment documents; <em>Outputs</em>: obligation and assignment records; <em>Validations</em>: an assignment is signed before anything relies on it.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-007\">INT-007</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-074\">FR-074</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Assistance is a last resort under statute, and seeking other income is a condition of eligibility (OB-EL-59).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-019",
     "anchor": "fr-019",
     "title": "Living in British Columbia and absences from it",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 8,
     "moduleText": "M8",
     "complexity": "Low",
     "lead": "The system records an absence from the province with its reason, timeframe and destination.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system records an absence from the province with its reason, timeframe and destination. It routes requests for a longer absence to the authorised approver. It makes an ineligibility decision based on absence only once the qualifying absence has actually happened, and only from the day policy sets.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-003\">BR-003</a>, UC-2</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-EL-21, OB-EL-22, OB-EL-23, OB-EL-24, OB-SU-25</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n20\">N20</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a recorded absence, when it has not reached the qualifying length, then no ineligibility can be recorded.</li><li>Given an ineligibility for absence, when the notice is generated, then it states the period of ineligibility the rule works out, not the whole absence.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: absence evidence; <em>Outputs</em>: absence determination; <em>Validations</em>: travel days counted as the rule says.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-061\">FR-061</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-063\">FR-063</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>A denial letter template in use today gets both the threshold and the period wrong (RC-06). The requirement follows the rule, not the template.</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-020",
     "anchor": "fr-020",
     "title": "Who is in the family unit, including spouses and dependants",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 8,
     "moduleText": "M8",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "The system decides who is in the family unit from recorded evidence.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system decides who is in the family unit from recorded evidence. It applies the spousal test to the evidence of financial and social interdependence at the time of assessment. It starts an eligibility review when a spouse is added. It supports eligibility for a child living apart from the family once efforts are recorded. It enforces the rules for returning and new members of transitional cases.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, UC-1, UC-2</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-EL-32, OB-EL-67, OB-SU-73, OB-SU-74, OB-SU-82</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n05\">N05</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n07\">N07</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a spouse added to a case, when the change is recorded, then an eligibility review work item is created.</li><li>Given a spousal determination, when it is recorded, then the evidence of financial and social interdependence it relied on is stored with it.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: household evidence; <em>Outputs</em>: family unit determination; <em>Validations</em>: membership carries effective dates.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-024\">FR-024</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Family unit composition drives every rate and most eligibility tests (OB-SU-73).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-021",
     "anchor": "fr-021",
     "title": "Clients on reserve, and designations made by another jurisdiction",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 8,
     "moduleText": "M8",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "The system routes people living on reserve, or on Modern Treaty land where the First Nation runs the program, to the First Nation, and records the evidence required for exceptions.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system routes people living on reserve, or on <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#modern-treaty\">Modern Treaty land</a> where the First Nation runs the program, to the First Nation, and records the evidence required for exceptions. It supports verification to the adjudicating body for on-reserve disability designation within the registered clock. It records a designation made by another jurisdiction as a recognised fact, shown as \"recognised as at date, unconfirmed since\".</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-008\">BR-008</a>, UC-1</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-EL-62, OB-EL-63, OB-IN-54</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n03\">N03</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n13\">N13</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given an applicant who lives where a First Nation runs the program, when intake runs, then the system routes them to the First Nation and records the routing.</li><li>Given a designation made in another jurisdiction, when the system relies on it, then the date it was recognised and how current it is are shown with it.</li><li>Given a verification request from the adjudicating body, when it arrives, then its registered clock starts and a breach is detected.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: residence evidence, outside designations; <em>Outputs</em>: routing and recognition records; <em>Validations</em>: consent recorded where sending the information requires it.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-036\">FR-036</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-012\">INT-012</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Each jurisdiction treats the other's determination as a prescribed-class fact, and neither side is told when the other withdraws a designation (OBLG §4.4; NOTE-004).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-022",
     "anchor": "fr-022",
     "title": "Sponsored immigrants",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 8,
     "moduleText": "M8",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "The system records efforts to contact sponsors for support.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system records efforts to contact sponsors for support. Where abuse concerns exist, it blocks all contact with the sponsor, including by letter, unless the sponsored person wants it. It routes cases with health or safety concerns to the responsible team.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-006\">BR-006</a>, UC-1</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-EL-65, OB-EL-66, OB-SU-69, OB-SU-70</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n21\">N21</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given an abuse concern recorded on a sponsorship case, when any letter or contact with the sponsor is generated or attempted, then it is blocked by default and the blocked attempt is recorded as an event.</li><li>Given a health or safety concern, when it is recorded, then a referral work item for the responsible team is created.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: sponsorship evidence, concern flags; <em>Outputs</em>: contact restrictions on the sponsor; <em>Validations</em>: the client's wishes are recorded before any restriction is lifted.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-080\">FR-080</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Policy restricts use of information in five ways, and barring contact with a particular person is one of them (PRIN <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n21\">N21</a>).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-023",
     "anchor": "fr-023",
     "title": "Child in the Home of a Relative",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 8,
     "moduleText": "M8",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "The system supports the rules of the Child in the Home of a Relative program, which is closed to new cases:",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system supports the rules of the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#cihr\">Child in the Home of a Relative</a> program, which is closed to new cases:</p><ul><li>screening consent from every adult in the home, as a condition of eligibility;</li><li>identity checks on the person submitting the form;</li><li>recording the submitter's ID numbers and the case numbers, without the child's name;</li><li>not keeping the screening consent form itself;</li><li>checking screening results daily;</li><li>approval before a case is closed or re-opened;</li><li>immediate referral of any child protection concern.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-006\">BR-006</a>, UC-2</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-EL-68, OB-EL-69, OB-EL-70, OB-EL-71, OB-EL-72, OB-EL-73, OB-EL-74, OB-EL-75</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n12\">N12</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n13\">N13</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a screening consent form, when it is processed, then its content is recorded as policy allows and the form itself is not kept.</li><li>Given a child protection concern on a case, when it is recorded, then a referral to the child protection authority is raised immediately and its routing is recorded.</li><li>Given a case, when someone tries to close or re-open it without the required approval, then the action is refused.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: screening consents and results; <em>Outputs</em>: eligibility evidence; <em>Validations</em>: the child's name is never stored on the consent record.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-010\">FR-010</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-070\">FR-070</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>The program runs on a frozen transition ruleset and has stricter privacy and child-safety rules than the general case (OBLG §6).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-024",
     "anchor": "fr-024",
     "title": "Scheduled reviews, recertifications and missed appointments",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 4,
     "moduleText": "M4, M8",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "The system schedules and runs every periodic review and recertification policy requires:",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system schedules and runs every periodic review and recertification policy requires: eligibility reviews, supplement reviews, recertifications, re-verification on each request, reviews triggered by age, and reviews of identity requirements. When a client does not attend, it issues the prescribed notice, cancels cheques, stops cheque production and closes the case.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-003\">BR-003</a>, UC-2</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-EL-25, OB-EL-35, OB-SU-23, OB-SU-26, OB-SU-35, OB-SU-47, OB-SU-48, OB-SU-49, OB-SU-81, OB-IN-57</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n20\">N20</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n05\">N05</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given each registered review type, when its clock reaches its trigger, then a review work item is created with its due date and <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#calendar-basis\">calendar basis</a>.</li><li>Given confirmed non-attendance at a mandatory review, when it is recorded, then the notice, the payment actions and the reconsideration clock follow as one recorded sequence.</li><li>Given an active investigation review on a case, when a scheduled review would start, then it is suspended as <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-054\">FR-054</a> requires, without telling the client.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: review schedule rules; <em>Outputs</em>: review work items and outcomes; <em>Validations</em>: each review type states its calendar basis.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-061\">FR-061</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-067\">FR-067</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Completing an eligibility review is mandatory, and not completing it ends eligibility (OB-EL-25). Review clocks run on seven different calendar bases (PRIN <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a>).</p>"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c-intake-identity-and-the-case",
   "title": "C. Intake, identity and the case",
   "intro": "",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "FR-025",
     "anchor": "fr-025",
     "title": "Taking an application in stages",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 3,
     "moduleText": "M3, M8",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "The system supports intake in stages.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system supports intake in stages. Stage one assesses work search or exemption and immediate need, and sets priority and the homelessness and fleeing-abuse indicators. Every adult then completes orientation, which covers the ministry's authority and the applicant's responsibilities. Stage two goes ahead once the required identification, shelter and income evidence is provided.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-009\">BR-009</a>, UC-1</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-IN-01, OB-IN-02, OB-IN-03, OB-IN-04, OB-IN-05, OB-IN-06, OB-IN-14, OB-IN-21</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n07\">N07</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n15\">N15</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given an applicant who says they are fleeing abuse, when stage one is recorded, then the application gets critical priority and the registered supervisor clock starts.</li><li>Given an applicant identified as homeless, when stage one is recorded, then the homeless indicator and its service standard apply.</li><li>Given a family unit, when stage two is scheduled, then every adult member's orientation is recorded first.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: application, disclosures; <em>Outputs</em>: stage <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#determination\">determinations</a>, indicators; <em>Validations</em>: a work-search exemption is stored as a recorded fact, not as the absence of records.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-067\">FR-067</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-071\">FR-071</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Intake is the front door, and policy sets its stages, clocks and priorities (OB-IN-01 to OB-IN-06).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-026",
     "anchor": "fr-026",
     "title": "Explaining rights, responsibilities and community resources, and recording it",
     "priority": "Should",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 8,
     "moduleText": "M8",
     "complexity": "Low",
     "lead": "The system prompts staff to explain rights, responsibilities, reporting duties, consents, notifications and privacy, and records that they did.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system prompts staff to explain rights, responsibilities, reporting duties, consents, notifications and privacy, and records that they did. It also records that the client was told about available community resources, exemptions and supplements. This applies at intake, for clients fleeing abuse, and during compliance review.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-003\">BR-003</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-009\">BR-009</a>, UC-1</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-EL-34, OB-IN-08, OB-IN-15, OB-IN-25, OB-IN-58</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n15\">N15</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n18\">N18</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given an intake or compliance review, when it is completed, then there is a record that each required explanation was given, by whom and when.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: checklist of explanations per event type; <em>Outputs</em>: record of explanations given; <em>Validations</em>: required items complete.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-032\">FR-032</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Policy requires both the explanation and a record of it. Without the record, nobody can show the explanation happened (OB-EL-34).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-027",
     "anchor": "fr-027",
     "title": "Establishing and proving identity",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 1,
     "moduleText": "M1",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "The system establishes identity before information is collected or released and before any signature is accepted.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system establishes identity before information is collected or released and before any signature is accepted. It supports:</p><ul><li>temporary assistance while identification or a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#federal-benefits\">SIN</a> is obtained, with its review clock;</li><li>the identity-proofing process for health coverage;</li><li>validation of mailed identity documents by a trusted third party;</li><li>a record of the client's name history;</li><li>a record of each step the client takes to get identification, without using third-party brokers.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-006\">BR-006</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-009\">BR-009</a>, UC-1</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-EL-70, OB-SU-71, OB-SU-72, OB-SU-75, OB-SU-86, OB-IN-13, OB-IN-55, OB-IN-56</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given any signature, including an electronic one, when identity has not been verified to the registered level, then the signature is not accepted.</li><li>Given assistance granted while identification is pending, when its registered period runs out, then a review with the approvals policy sets is required.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: identity evidence; <em>Outputs</em>: <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#identity-assurance\">identity assurance level</a> on the person's record; <em>Validations</em>: assurance level recorded for each method.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-028\">FR-028</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-005\">INT-005</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Signatures and disclosures are invalid unless the right person is identified (OB-IN-13, OB-IN-33).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-028",
     "anchor": "fr-028",
     "title": "One client index, with people deciding uncertain matches",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 1,
     "moduleText": "M1",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "The system provides a client index that matches people by exact rules and by likelihood, and sends uncertain matches to a queue where a person decides.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system provides a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#client-index\">client index</a> that matches people by exact rules and by likelihood, and sends uncertain matches to a queue where a person decides. The index holds only identifiers and the details needed for matching; it does not become a second copy of the identity directory.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-011\">BR-011</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-012\">BR-012</a>, UC-1</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n03\">N03</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n05\">N05</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a new applicant, when a probable match to an existing person falls below the automatic-link threshold, then a match <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#work-item\">work item</a> is raised for a person to decide.</li><li>Given any merge or split of records, when it is done, then it is recorded as an adjudication, with the decision-maker.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: personal details used for matching; <em>Outputs</em>: person references; <em>Validations</em>: no automatic merge of records that affect a client.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/data#dr-019\">DR-019</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>No off-the-shelf search product matches people with a human review queue, so the architecture names this as one of the few pieces to build (TA §C.18.1).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-029",
     "anchor": "fr-029",
     "title": "Health coverage",
     "priority": "Should",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 8,
     "moduleText": "M8",
     "complexity": "Low",
     "lead": "Where policy requires it, the system makes sure health coverage is applied for on a recipient's behalf.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Where policy requires it, the system makes sure health coverage is applied for on a recipient's behalf. It records reported changes to name, sex or birth date for the health insurer. It supports the identity-proofing process for new and returning residents, with its period of pre-authorised coverage.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, UC-1</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-SU-53, OB-SU-54, OB-SU-83</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n06\">N06</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n13\">N13</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given an eligible recipient without coverage, when assistance is granted, then a coverage application work item or data exchange is created.</li><li>Given pre-authorised coverage awaiting verification, when its registered period runs out, then the verification status is shown to the worker.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: coverage status (<a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-008\">INT-008</a>); <em>Outputs</em>: coverage actions; <em>Validations</em>: changes are passed on to the insurer.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-008\">INT-008</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Health coverage depends on assistance status, and another program runs it (OB-SU-83).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-030",
     "anchor": "fr-030",
     "title": "Disability (PWD) and persistent-barriers (PPMB) designation",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 8,
     "moduleText": "M8",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "The system supports applying for, and deciding, disability and persistent-multiple-barriers designation, including the prescribed classes where another body establishes the designation.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system supports applying for, and deciding, disability and persistent-multiple-barriers designation, including the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#prescribed-class\">prescribed classes</a> where another body establishes the designation. An application can go forward only once intake is complete, the application is signed and a case is open. The deciding team and its decision are recorded.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-014\">BR-014</a>, UC-1</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-IN-52</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n20\">N20</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a designation application, when intake is incomplete or the application is unsigned, then it cannot be sent for a decision.</li><li>Given a prescribed-class application, when consent is recorded, then verification with the named agency is requested and its result is recorded as evidence.</li><li>Given a designation decision, when it is recorded, then its <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#adjudicability\">adjudicability</a> attributes are read from the register (<a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-092\">FR-092</a>).</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: application, professional reports; <em>Outputs</em>: designation determination; <em>Validations</em>: the deciding authority is recorded.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-036\">FR-036</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-092\">FR-092</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Designation is a statutory decision under the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#ea-acts\">EAPWD Act</a>. <strong>Open items</strong>: policy sets no time limit for deciding an application, and sets no criteria, decision-maker, notice or clock for rescinding a designation <span class=\"cite\">OBLG-C7</span>. Both need ministry rulings before this requirement is complete.</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-031",
     "anchor": "fr-031",
     "title": "Employability plans",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 8,
     "moduleText": "M8",
     "complexity": "Low",
     "lead": "The system records employability plans and their conditions.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system records employability plans and their conditions. It supports going over the plan with the client and giving them a copy. It requires the client's acknowledgement whenever the plan changes.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, UC-2</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-IN-48, OB-IN-50</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n20\">N20</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a changed plan, when it is saved, then it does not take effect until the client's acknowledgement is recorded.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: plan terms; <em>Outputs</em>: versioned plan with acknowledgements; <em>Validations</em>: each version has an effective date.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-074\">FR-074</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>A non-compliance decision can only be defended against a plan the client acknowledged (OB-IN-49, OB-IN-50).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-032",
     "anchor": "fr-032",
     "title": "A complete case record, so work can continue",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 4,
     "moduleText": "M4",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "The system records decisions, contacts and actions on the case so that another staff member can pick up the work without asking the client again.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system records decisions, contacts and actions on the case so that another staff member can pick up the work without asking the client again.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-012\">BR-012</a>, UC-1</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-IN-16, OB-IN-26</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n04\">N04</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given any work item handed to another worker, when they open it, then the decisions, contacts and pending actions are visible without looking in another system.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: case activity; <em>Outputs</em>: case history view; <em>Validations</em>: case notes are stored in a form that allows parts to be severed (<a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-078\">FR-078</a>).</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-067\">FR-067</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Policy requires records good enough for someone else to continue the work (OB-IN-16).</p>"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "d-supplements-and-hardship",
   "title": "D. Supplements and hardship",
   "intro": "",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "FR-033",
     "anchor": "fr-033",
     "title": "A catalogue of entitlements, with rules for each variant",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 5,
     "moduleText": "M5, M8",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "Every supplement and program entitlement is an entry in a catalogue.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Every supplement and program entitlement is an entry in a catalogue. Each entry holds its <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#variant\">variants</a>, rules, rates, caps, replacement intervals, deciding authority and <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#adjudicability\">adjudicability</a>, and nothing is assumed from a parent entry. The catalogue also holds the rules for items the ministry never pays for, and for when the client pays amounts above the allowed rates.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-003\">BR-003</a>, UC-3</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-SU-17, OB-SU-24, OB-SU-55, OB-SU-84, OB-SU-85</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n04\">N04</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n20\">N20</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a variant entry, when any attribute is left unstated, then the entry is incomplete and cannot be released. Silence on a variant's page is not inheritance from its parent <span class=\"cite\">PRIN-C2</span>.</li><li>Given a request for an item the catalogue marks as never paid by the ministry, when it is processed, then no <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#payment-instruction\">payment instruction</a> can be created for it.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: policy pages; <em>Outputs</em>: catalogue entries; <em>Validations</em>: every attribute present for every variant.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-090\">FR-090</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-092\">FR-092</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>About forty-five supplements each have their own tests, rates, caps, routes and intervals. Treating them as generic financial components loses all of that (GAPS P-05).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-034",
     "anchor": "fr-034",
     "title": "Approval before the cost is incurred",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 6,
     "moduleText": "M6, M8",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Some entitlements need approval before the client incurs the cost:",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Some entitlements need approval before the client incurs the cost: medical equipment, breathing devices, medical transportation, burial or cremation, and moving costs. For these, the system requires an approval decision first. It refuses payment for purchases made without approval, except under the registered emergency exception.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-004\">BR-004</a>, UC-3</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-SU-14, OB-SU-27, OB-SU-37, OB-SU-41, OB-SU-56</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n07\">N07</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n20\">N20</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given an invoice for an entitlement that needs approval first, when no approval is dated before the purchase, then no payment instruction can be created unless the emergency exception is recorded with its authority.</li><li>Given an approval with an expiry date, when it expires, then a new application is required.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: approval decisions, invoices; <em>Outputs</em>: authorised payments; <em>Validations</em>: approval date comes before purchase date.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-042\">FR-042</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-050\">FR-050</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Policy says the ministry is not responsible for paying for purchases made without approval (OB-SU-37, OB-SU-41).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-035",
     "anchor": "fr-035",
     "title": "Health supplements: medical evidence and replacement intervals",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 8,
     "moduleText": "M8",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "The system records the medical documents each health supplement requires, from the kinds of professional policy names.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system records the medical documents each health supplement requires, from the kinds of professional policy names. It enforces the replacement interval for each kind of item, requires other available resources to be considered first, and enforces the rules that allow only one of several nutrition-related supplements.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, UC-3</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-SU-28, OB-SU-44, OB-SU-45, OB-SU-46, OB-SU-50, OB-SU-51, OB-SU-52, OB-SU-88</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n07\">N07</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a request made inside an item's replacement interval, when it is assessed, then the interval rule is applied and cited in the decision.</li><li>Given medical documentation, when it is recorded, then the author's profession is recorded and checked against the professions accepted for that entitlement.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: medical evidence; <em>Outputs</em>: entitlement decisions; <em>Validations</em>: author's profession, document date.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-033\">FR-033</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Each health supplement item has its own documentation and interval rules (OB-SU-44 to OB-SU-52).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-036",
     "anchor": "fr-036",
     "title": "Entitlements decided by other bodies",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 5,
     "moduleText": "M5, M8",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "The system records each body that makes decisions, whether a ministry unit or an outside body such as Pacific Blue Cross, CLBC or BC Children's Hospital.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system records each body that makes decisions, whether a ministry unit or an outside body such as <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#pbc-clbc\">Pacific Blue Cross</a>, CLBC or BC Children's Hospital. For each it records:</p><ul><li>what it may decide;</li><li>whether it decides, reviews, or both;</li><li>whether and for how long its decisions are recognised;</li><li>what it must send back to the ministry.</li></ul><p>The system takes in that body's decisions as evidence with their source recorded. It records any ministry replacement interval the body's decision uses up.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-002\">BR-002</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-003\">BR-003</a>, UC-3</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-SU-36, OB-SU-43</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n02\">N02</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n05\">N05</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n20\">N20</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given an entitlement whose first decision is delegated to another body, when a request comes directly to the ministry, then it is routed as policy says, including refusing direct requests the ministry does not accept.</li><li>Given an outside body's decision, when it is taken in, then it reads as a decision by a named authority, with its adjudicability, not as a bare fact <span class=\"cite\">NOTE4-C1</span>.</li><li>Given an entitlement where both deciding and reviewing are delegated, when the client asks to appeal, then the rights text directs them to that body.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: outside decisions (<a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-009\">INT-009</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-010\">INT-010</a>); <em>Outputs</em>: recognised decisions, a record of used-up intervals; <em>Validations</em>: the body is allowed to decide that entitlement.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-009\">INT-009</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-010\">INT-010</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-092\">FR-092</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Eleven entitlements are first decided outside the ministry, and the ministry's own clocks tick where only the administrator can see them <span class=\"cite\">MAP-C2</span>.</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-037",
     "anchor": "fr-037",
     "title": "Automatic and seasonal payments",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 6,
     "moduleText": "M6",
     "complexity": "Low",
     "lead": "Some entitlements, such as the Winter Supplement, are paid automatically in a set window.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Some entitlements, such as the Winter Supplement, are paid automatically in a set window. The system includes them in the right payment for every eligible recipient without a request, and does not allow them to be issued outside their window.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, UC-6</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-SU-10, OB-SU-11</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n04\">N04</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given the registered payment window, when the run for it is assembled, then every eligible recipient's payment instruction includes the component.</li><li>Given any other period, when a worker tries to issue it, then the attempt is refused.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: eligibility, window rule; <em>Outputs</em>: components on payment instructions; <em>Validations</em>: window taken from the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#rules-register\">rules register</a>.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-043\">FR-043</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Policy both requires automatic payment and forbids payment at other times (OB-SU-10, OB-SU-11).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-038",
     "anchor": "fr-038",
     "title": "Burial and cremation",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 8,
     "moduleText": "M8",
     "complexity": "Low",
     "lead": "The system pays approved burial or cremation costs only after eligibility is confirmed and the legal representative has decided the final arrangements, and never before a death.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system pays approved burial or cremation costs only after eligibility is confirmed and the legal representative has decided the final arrangements, and never before a death. It starts cost recovery wherever policy allows.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-004\">BR-004</a>, UC-3</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-SU-12, OB-SU-13, OB-SU-15</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a burial request, when no date of death is recorded, then no payment instruction can be created.</li><li>Given a paid burial, when the deceased's estate or other sources can repay the cost, then a recovery <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#work-item\">work item</a> is created.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: evidence of death, legal representative's decision; <em>Outputs</em>: payment and recovery records; <em>Validations</em>: events must happen in the required order.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-034\">FR-034</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-016\">INT-016</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>These are policy rules about the order of events, with no time limit, so the system enforces the order (OB-SU-15).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-039",
     "anchor": "fr-039",
     "title": "Crisis supplements",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 8,
     "moduleText": "M8",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Once a client is found eligible for a crisis supplement, the system authorises the cheapest option that meets the need.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Once a client is found eligible for a crisis supplement, the system authorises the cheapest option that meets the need. It allows emergency and disaster crisis supplements only under the authority policy names. It starts a case review when a client reaches the registered pattern of repeated reliance.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, UC-3</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-SU-01, OB-SU-02, OB-SU-03</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n07\">N07</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a crisis decision, when options are compared, then the option chosen and the options considered are recorded.</li><li>Given the registered count of crisis supplements within the rolling period, when it is reached, then a review work item for repeated reliance is created.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: need, options and costs; <em>Outputs</em>: crisis decision; <em>Validations</em>: the rolling-period count follows the clock's <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#calendar-basis\">calendar basis</a>.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-050\">FR-050</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-061\">FR-061</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Choosing the cheapest option needs a list of options and a price model, and no part of the system owns those today (MAP part 3, G-SU-01).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-040",
     "anchor": "fr-040",
     "title": "Hardship assistance",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 8,
     "moduleText": "M8",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "The system supports hardship assistance for each category.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system supports hardship assistance for each category. It records that alternatives were exhausted and documents the efforts made. It reassesses monthly and when the reason for hardship ends. It tells the client about any time limits when they apply, closes the case after the registered number of consecutive months, and requires supervisor approval to extend. Monthly re-checks do not depend on how the client is paid.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-009\">BR-009</a>, UC-1, UC-6</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-SU-57, OB-SU-58, OB-SU-59, OB-SU-60, OB-SU-61, OB-SU-62, OB-SU-63, OB-SU-65, OB-SU-68</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n15\">N15</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a hardship case, when its monthly reassessment is due, then a re-check work item is created, whatever the payment channel.</li><li>Given a category with a time limit, when the limit is reached, then an extension needs the recorded approval policy names.</li><li>Given a category that forbids paying a landlord directly, when such a payment instruction is proposed, then it is refused.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: hardship category, evidence of alternatives; <em>Outputs</em>: monthly decisions; <em>Validations</em>: the order of categories follows the rules register.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-024\">FR-024</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-044\">FR-044</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Policy currently uses sending cheques to an office as the monthly re-check <span class=\"cite\">PRIN-C8</span>. The duty to reach clients and the re-check must be separated (Conflict C-3).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-041",
     "anchor": "fr-041",
     "title": "Money paid out now that may have to be repaid",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 6,
     "moduleText": "M6, M7",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Some money is paid out against a signed promise to repay:",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Some money is paid out against a signed promise to repay: reconsideration and appeal supplements, security and pet deposits, co-op share purchases, warrant-related supplements, and hardship promises to pay. The system records each as a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#repayable\">repayable issuance</a>. It holds the signed promise, the decision it is waiting on and the outcome. It becomes a debt only on the outcome policy sets.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-004\">BR-004</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-005\">BR-005</a>, UC-4, UC-5</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-R18, OB-A11, OB-EL-38, OB-SU-04, OB-SU-06, OB-SU-07, OB-SU-08, OB-SU-67</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n05\">N05</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a repayable issuance, when the promise to repay is not signed, then no payment instruction issues.</li><li>Given the decision it is waiting on, when that decision issues, then the repayable issuance settles automatically as closed, partly repayable or fully repayable, with no manual reconciliation.</li><li>Given deposit rules that depend on earlier deposits still owing, when a new deposit is requested, then the rule is applied using the recorded repayable issuances.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: signed promise, reference to the awaited decision; <em>Outputs</em>: settlement events; <em>Validations</em>: settled only by the linked decision.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-042\">FR-042</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-053\">FR-053</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Money paid now, whose repayment depends on a later decision, fits neither the payment model nor the overpayment model <span class=\"cite\">NOTE5-C1</span>. Whether an appeal supplement must be repaid when the appeal is dismissed has been referred to the ministry, and the model must support either answer.</p>"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "e-payments-and-financial-control",
   "title": "E. Payments and financial control",
   "intro": "",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "FR-042",
     "anchor": "fr-042",
     "title": "Every payment goes through one issuance service",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 0,
     "moduleText": "M0 (specification and criteria 1–3), M6",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "Every payment of public money starts as a payment instruction created from a determination.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Every payment of public money starts as a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#payment-instruction\">payment instruction</a> created from a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#determination\">determination</a>. Once accepted, an instruction cannot be changed. It carries an identifier the system can recalculate, the determinations it pays, the payee and the capacity they are paid in, the gross amount with each deduction listed, the value date, the benefit period, the channel, a purpose code, a funding code, and the requester and approver. Every instruction passes through one <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#issuance-service\">Issuance Service</a>. No other component holds a credential for a payment rail, a cheque print stream or the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#cas\">corporate financial system</a>'s posting interface.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-004\">BR-004</a>, UC-6</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n05\">N05</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n18\">N18</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given the credential inventory and the build, when any module outside the Issuance Service declares a dependency on a payment rail, print or posting client, then the build fails (an automated architecture test).</li><li>Given an instruction identifier that already exists, when it is submitted again, then no second payment is created, whether or not the details match; if the details differ, the submission is rejected with a reason.</li><li>Given an instruction with no determination reference, when it is submitted, then it is flagged as an exception and needs the exception approval.</li><li>Given an accepted instruction, when a change is needed, then it is cancelled and replaced, or stopped and reissued. It is never edited.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: <code>DeterminationIssued</code> events. <em>Outputs</em>: payment instructions. <em>Validations</em>: the identifier is derived from the determination reference, benefit period, payee reference and instruction sequence.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-043\">FR-043</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-046\">FR-046</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-001\">INT-001</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>A chokepoint that is stated but never specified cannot be built. Adding one after three contexts already hold their own payment-rail credentials means accrediting the payment path all over again <span class=\"cite\">TA-C4</span>.</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-043",
     "anchor": "fr-043",
     "title": "Issuance runs",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 6,
     "moduleText": "M6",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "Payments are issued in runs.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Payments are issued in runs. A run is scheduled, can be resumed, can be audited, and follows a published calendar. Its stages are: cycle open, cutoff, assembly and pre-flight checks, <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#control-totals\">control totals</a> set before approval, approval, release, settlement and returns, reconciliation, and close. A run can be released more than once without paying twice. Supplementary and off-cycle payments are a run of one, with the same controls.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-004\">BR-004</a>, UC-6</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n09\">N09</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a release interrupted part-way, when it resumes, then it finishes instruction by instruction without paying anything twice, and the control totals match those set before approval <span class=\"cite\">TA-C17</span>.</li><li>Given pre-flight exceptions above the published threshold, when assembly finishes, then the run does not proceed.</li><li>Given a closed run, when an adjustment is needed, then it is made with new instructions, and the run cannot be reopened.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: the set of instructions selected by query, and the cycle definition version. <em>Outputs</em>: a run record with frozen totals. <em>Validations</em>: thresholds are policy settings, not values written into code.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-042\">FR-042</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-045\">FR-045</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-009\">FR-009</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>The dangerous failure is a run that stops halfway. An operator under pressure then runs it again and pays a live caseload twice (TA §C.6.2).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-044",
     "anchor": "fr-044",
     "title": "Payment channels, stop, recall, reissue and returns",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 0,
     "moduleText": "M0 (returns handling), M6",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "The system pays by direct deposit, by cheque and through the province's approved payment service.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system pays by direct deposit, by cheque and through the province's approved payment service. Stop payment, recall, reissue and return are four separate operations, each with its own states. The system refuses to reissue a payment unless the original is stopped, returned or rejected. When a payment is returned, the system marks the entitlement as unpaid and queues a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#work-item\">work item</a>. It starts electronic traces, and it applies a client's choice of payment channel by the cut-off policy sets.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-004\">BR-004</a>, UC-6</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-SU-29, OB-SU-30, OB-SU-31, OB-SU-34</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n05\">N05</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n06\">N06</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a stop request, when the channel reports failure, then the state is \"stop failed\" and no reissue is permitted.</li><li>Given a failed recall, when it is recorded, then the move to an overpayment is recorded as an event, not re-keyed by hand.</li><li>Given a returned payment, when it arrives, then the entitlement is marked unpaid and a work item with its service level is created.</li><li>Given a lost or stolen cheque, when a replacement is requested, then the policy conditions (including any service provider signature) are met before it is reissued.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: channel acknowledgements and return files. <em>Outputs</em>: channel states and links from each reissue to its original. <em>Validations</em>: a reissue never creates a second entitlement.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-042\">FR-042</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-002\">INT-002</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-003\">INT-003</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>If a system can pay but cannot find and resend failed payments, some clients go unpaid and nobody notices (TA §C.6.3).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-045",
     "anchor": "fr-045",
     "title": "Benefit ledger and three-way reconciliation",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 6,
     "moduleText": "M6",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "The system keeps its own double-entry ledger of benefit obligations, recorded when they are owed.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system keeps its own double-entry <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#ledger\">ledger</a> of benefit obligations, recorded when they are owed. It records each obligation raised, each payment released and settled, each reversal, each debt raised, each recovery and each write-off. Every entry carries the coding block, the determination reference and the run identifier. Each day the system reconciles the ledger against the channels' settlement records and against the corporate financial system. Each cycle it checks that every financial determination has an obligation and every obligation has a determination.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-004\">BR-004</a>, UC-6</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n18\">N18</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n04\">N04</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given any unmatched item, when reconciliation runs, then a break record is created with an owner, an age and an escalation threshold.</li><li>Given a financial determination with no obligation, or an obligation with no determination, when the cycle's reconciliation runs, then it raises an alarm at once.</li><li>Given a full monthly cycle at production volume on <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#deidentified\">synthetic</a> data, when it is reconciled, then there are no unexplained breaks.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: ledger entries, settlement files, corporate postings. <em>Outputs</em>: reconciliation and break feeds. <em>Validations</em>: control totals do not change after assembly.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-042\">FR-042</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-001\">INT-001</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-002\">INT-002</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>The corporate financial system stays the book of record. The third check, determinations against obligations, is the one that catches the architecture's central claim failing (TA §C.6.4).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-046",
     "anchor": "fr-046",
     "title": "Separation of duties enforced in code",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 0,
     "moduleText": "M0 (specification), M6",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "No person or program can both start and approve a payment.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>No person or program can both start and approve a payment. The system refuses a run's approval if the approver requested any instruction in it, or if the approver's delegated authority is below the run's net value. Changes to a payee's bank details made within the registered window before a run are held for a second approval. Only a separate role can change channel settings.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-004\">BR-004</a>, UC-6</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a realistic run in a test environment, when someone who created an instruction in it tries to approve it, then the service refuses, logs the attempt, and the refusal appears in the audit stream with no person stepping in <span class=\"cite\">TA-C18</span>.</li><li>Given a payee account change inside the hold window, when the next run is assembled, then the affected instruction is held until a second person approves it.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: the delegated authority schedule. <em>Outputs</em>: refusal events. <em>Validations</em>: authority limits are effective-dated.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-094\">FR-094</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>A control left to process only holds until it is tested by pressure (PRIN <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a>).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-047",
     "anchor": "fr-047",
     "title": "Emergency payments and interim provider payments",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 0,
     "moduleText": "M0 (design and rehearsal), M6 (exercise)",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "The system has a designed emergency payment path.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system has a designed emergency payment path. Clients receive <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#emergency-issuance\">emergency issuance</a>; providers receive interim payments. The path skips only the automated determination. A worker with stated authority pays an amount against a named statutory head, and the system records this as a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#discretionary\">discretionary determination</a>. The payment still goes through the same chokepoint, ledger, control totals and <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#separation-of-duties\">separation of duties</a>. Each emergency payment creates an obligation to reconcile it later against the real determination. The path has ceilings per cycle and per client, measurable triggers, and a time limit on each use.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-004\">BR-004</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-013\">BR-013</a>, UC-6</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n16\">N16</a> [PROPOSED], <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a registered trigger, when the authorised role invokes emergency issuance, then the invocation ends at the end of the cycle unless someone invokes it again with a written reason.</li><li>Given any emergency or interim instruction, when the determination is later made, then the system calculates and classifies the difference automatically and raises a reconciliation work item with its service level.</li><li>Given the path's stated capacity, when it is load-tested, then it carries the stated share of a program's caseload for the stated number of days. This is exercised before M6 ends.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: authority, statutory head, reason. <em>Outputs</em>: emergency instructions with purpose codes. <em>Validations</em>: ceilings are reference data.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-042\">FR-042</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-043\">FR-043</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-051\">FR-051</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>A <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#rollback\">rollback</a> restores the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#system-of-record\">system of record</a> over days, but a client's rent is due on a set date. An emergency path invented under pressure cannot be reconciled afterwards <span class=\"cite\">TA-C5</span>.</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-048",
     "anchor": "fr-048",
     "title": "Deductions, set-off and the minimum amount a client must keep",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 6,
     "moduleText": "M6",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Recovery reduces the net amount of a payment instruction.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Recovery reduces the net amount of a payment instruction. It appears as a listed deduction and never as a lower gross amount. The system checks the statutory minimum a client must keep when it issues each payment, and the chokepoint refuses any deduction that would go below it. <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#set-off\">Set-off</a> across programs happens only through Overpayment and Recovery and the chokepoint.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-004\">BR-004</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-005\">BR-005</a>, UC-5, UC-6</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-SU-09</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n03\">N03</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given an agreed recovery rate, when a client's entitlement falls so the rate would go below the minimum, then the deduction is reduced to the minimum when the payment is issued, and the reason is recorded.</li><li>Given any deduction, when the notice is issued, then the deduction appears as its own line.</li><li>Given a case context, when it tries to set off directly against another context's entitlement, then the operation is not available.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: repayment agreements and the minimum-amount rule. <em>Outputs</em>: deduction lines. <em>Validations</em>: the minimum comes from the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#rules-register\">rules register</a>.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-042\">FR-042</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-053\">FR-053</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>If a deduction engine can be set below the minimum, someone will eventually do it in a hurry for a whole group of clients (TA §C.7.3).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-049",
     "anchor": "fr-049",
     "title": "Tax information slips",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 6,
     "moduleText": "M6",
     "complexity": "Low",
     "lead": "The system issues the tax information slip policy requires to every recipient above the registered threshold for the tax year.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system issues the tax information slip policy requires to every recipient above the registered threshold for the tax year. It takes the figures from the ledger's payment records.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-004\">BR-004</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-IN-32</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n06\">N06</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n09\">N09</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a tax year's settled payments, when slips are generated, then each slip matches the ledger for that recipient and year.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: the ledger. <em>Outputs</em>: slips and filing. <em>Validations</em>: the threshold comes from the rules register.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-045\">FR-045</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>This is a statutory reporting duty, met from the book of record (OB-IN-32).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-050",
     "anchor": "fr-050",
     "title": "Managing and paying providers",
     "priority": "Should",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 6,
     "moduleText": "M6",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "The system records recognised providers and the principles used to recognise a type of provider.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system records recognised providers and the principles used to recognise a type of provider. It proposes contracted providers first where policy says so. It records provider confirmations and client acknowledgements at delivery, and enforces provider obligations such as trial periods and supplies that must come with an item. It pays providers through the chokepoint.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-004\">BR-004</a>, UC-3</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-SU-16, OB-SU-33, OB-SU-39, OB-SU-40, OB-SU-42</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n03\">N03</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n11\">N11</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given an equipment purchase, when a contracted provider exists for that type of item, then the contracted provider is proposed first and any exception is recorded.</li><li>Given delivery of equipment that needs the client's signed acknowledgement, when the acknowledgement is missing, then the provider's invoice cannot be paid.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: the provider registry and invoices. <em>Outputs</em>: provider payment instructions. <em>Validations</em>: the provider's recognition is current on the date of service.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-020\">INT-020</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-042\">FR-042</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Provider and Outcome Management has its own obligations, and a current system the architecture never specified (APP §5).</p>"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "f-overpayment-compliance-and-investigation",
   "title": "F. Overpayment, compliance and investigation",
   "intro": "",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "FR-051",
     "anchor": "fr-051",
     "title": "Overpayments calculated and classified from the evidence that changed",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 6,
     "moduleText": "M6",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "An overpayment is the difference between two determination records for the same period.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>An overpayment is the difference between two <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#determination\">determination</a> records for the same period. The system splits it into one component for each change in evidence. It classifies each component by the operation and fault recorded on that change:</p><ul><li>a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#correction\">supersession</a>, or a correction where the client was at fault, is recoverable;</li><li>a correction where the ministry was at fault is <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#overpayment\">administrative error</a>;</li><li>where a third party was at fault, a person decides, and the default is administrative error;</li><li>where fault cannot be determined, it is administrative error unless a person reclassifies it.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-005\">BR-005</a>, UC-5</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n06\">N06</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a recalculation with components in more than one class, when the overpayment is raised, then each component has its own classification and recovery terms, and the notice states each one separately.</li><li>Given a migrated fact where nobody knows when the ministry learned it, when a component depends on it, then the component defaults to administrative error and is not recovered unless a person reclassifies it on recorded evidence <span class=\"cite\">TA-C19</span>.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: two <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#decision-record\">determination records</a> and the evidence events. <em>Outputs</em>: classified components. <em>Validations</em>: classification is required; an unclassified component cannot be acted on.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-012\">FR-012</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/data#dr-013\">DR-013</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>The same arithmetic can be a recoverable debt in one case and an administrative error in another. What decides it is what changed in the evidence (TA §C.7.2). Legal counsel owns the question of how each class is treated under the statute.</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-052",
     "anchor": "fr-052",
     "title": "A person decides every debt; raising is capped, grouped by cause and reversible",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 0,
     "moduleText": "M0 (reversal mechanism), M6",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "No overpayment is raised and no recovery starts unless a person decides each component.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>No overpayment is raised and no recovery starts unless a person decides each component. Automated raising has a cap per cycle on count and on value. When a single cause produces overpayments for more clients than the published threshold, the whole group is held for review before any notice goes out. A batch of debts can be reversed in one operation. The reversal also undoes recovery already taken and issues corrected notices.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-005\">BR-005</a>, UC-5</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n18\">N18</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n14\">N14</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a calculated component, when no person has recorded a decision, then no debt, notice or recovery exists <span class=\"cite\">TA-C6</span>.</li><li>Given automated raising that exceeds its cap in a cycle, when the cap is reached, then raising stops and escalates rather than queuing.</li><li>Given a batch identifier, when reversal is invoked, then every debt, deduction, <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#set-off\">set-off</a> and collections referral from that batch is reversed, and corrected notices are issued.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: components and the group-review thresholds. <em>Outputs</em>: debts and reversal events. <em>Validations</em>: thresholds are set before the first live determination.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-051\">FR-051</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-060\">FR-060</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>A defect that produces a hundred thousand wrong records shows up as one pattern repeated. A process that looks only at one case at a time will never see it (TA §C.7.6).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-053",
     "anchor": "fr-053",
     "title": "Repayment, write-off, collections and disputes",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 6,
     "moduleText": "M6",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Repayment agreements keep a version history.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Repayment agreements keep a version history. Where policy requires it, repayment continues after a recipient leaves assistance. A write-off needs one person to request it and a different person, with authority at the threshold, to approve it. A write-off never deletes the overpayment record. A debt referred to collections can be recalled in one operation. A client may dispute whether the debt exists, the amount, the classification or the terms. Each kind of dispute follows the route the architecture sets. Recovery pauses by default while the determination or the classification is disputed.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-005\">BR-005</a>, UC-5</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-SU-05</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a dispute of the underlying determination, when it is recorded, then recovery pauses by default, and only a named authority can change that default.</li><li>Given a referred debt that is reduced on appeal, when the outcome is recorded, then the referral is recalled in one operation.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: agreements, disputes, write-off requests. <em>Outputs</em>: <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#ledger\">ledger</a> events. <em>Validations</em>: write-off thresholds are reference data.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-045\">FR-045</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-019\">INT-019</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>The most common collections complaint in this area is a debt that was disputed or reduced after referral and never withdrawn (TA §C.7.4).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-054",
     "anchor": "fr-054",
     "title": "Allegations, investigations and referral to investigators",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 6,
     "moduleText": "M6, M8",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Staff can refer suspected fraud, duplicate identification or long-term ineligibility to the investigation unit, including on closed cases.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Staff can refer suspected fraud, duplicate identification or long-term ineligibility to the investigation unit, including on closed cases. Current eligibility must be assessed first. While an investigation is open, it blocks other work as policy requires, and the system hides it from the client and from staff who do not need to know. The system prevents direct confrontation or contact where policy forbids it, and records the outcome of each investigation.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-005\">BR-005</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-006\">BR-006</a>, UC-2</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-EL-13, OB-EL-14, OB-EL-31, OB-EL-33, OB-IN-44, OB-IN-45, OB-IN-46, OB-IN-59, OB-IN-60</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n05\">N05</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n21\">N21</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given an open investigation on a case, when a worker opens the case, then the system blocks disclosing the investigation to the client and routes the client's questions about it to the investigation office.</li><li>Given a suspicion of personation or duplicate identification, when it is recorded, then a referral is created at once and contact with the client about it is blocked.</li><li>Given a referral, when current eligibility has not been assessed, then the referral cannot be submitted.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: allegations and data matches. <em>Outputs</em>: referrals and investigation status. <em>Validations</em>: referral content follows policy.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-080\">FR-080</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-070\">FR-070</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>An open investigation holds up work in other contexts and continues after a case closes. The mapping found that no context owned it (NOTE-003: Investigation and Loss Management).</p>"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g-reconsideration-and-appeal",
   "title": "G. Reconsideration and appeal",
   "intro": "",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "FR-055",
     "anchor": "fr-055",
     "title": "Every reconsideration request is accepted and recorded",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 7,
     "moduleText": "M7 (M2 for the screens that take requests)",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "A client may ask for reconsideration of any communication, on any channel, including when the ministry thinks no decision has been made.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>A client may ask for reconsideration of any communication, on any channel, including when the ministry thinks no decision has been made. The system records every request with the date and channel it arrived by. No path in the system lets staff turn a request away when it is made.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-003\">BR-003</a>, UC-4</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-R14, OB-R15</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n15\">N15</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given any client-facing channel and any communication, when a client asks for reconsideration, then the request is recorded with the date received and the channel <span class=\"cite\">NOTE1-C1</span>.</li><li>Given a worker or contact centre screen, when a request comes in, then there is no control to refuse it, only to record and route it.</li><li>Given a request made on paper or in person, when it is recorded later, then its received date is the day it physically arrived.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: the request, and a reference to what it is about (which may be something the ministry does not consider a decision). <em>Outputs</em>: a request record that starts the decision on whether reconsideration is available. <em>Validations</em>: received date and channel are required.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-056\">FR-056</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-071\">FR-071</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Policy gives an unconditional right to ask. Telling a client \"there is nothing to reconsider\" is a defect in practice (Conflict C-1) <span class=\"cite\">OBLG-C4</span>.</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-056",
     "anchor": "fr-056",
     "title": "The independent unit decides whether reconsideration is available",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 7,
     "moduleText": "M7",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Whether reconsideration is available is an adjudication.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Whether reconsideration is available is an adjudication. The <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#rafu\">Reconsideration and Administrative Fairness Unit</a> makes it, modelled as an <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#adjudicating-authority\">adjudicating authority</a> that holds that power. The officer who issued the communication never makes it.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-003\">BR-003</a>, UC-4</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-R16</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n05\">N05</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n20\">N20</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a request, when availability is decided, then the person deciding belongs to the independent unit and took no part in the original communication.</li><li>Given a finding that reconsideration is not available, when the client is told, then the notice states the finding and the reasons.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: the request and the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#adjudicability\">adjudicability</a> attributes. <em>Outputs</em>: the availability decision. <em>Validations</em>: the person deciding took no part in the original.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-036\">FR-036</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-092\">FR-092</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>If the context that runs reconsiderations also decided availability, it would rule on its own jurisdiction (NOTE-001 v2.0).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-057",
     "anchor": "fr-057",
     "title": "Reconsideration is a new decision by an independent officer",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 7,
     "moduleText": "M7",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "A reconsideration is a new decision on the whole matter.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>A reconsideration is a new decision on the whole matter. An officer who took no part in the original decision makes it, using the evidence held when the decision is made. The system supports both kinds of extension, each with its own authorisation. A ministry-side extension without its required authorisation is invalid.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-003\">BR-003</a>, UC-4</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-R01, OB-R02, OB-R06, OB-R07, OB-R08</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n05\">N05</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n09\">N09</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given an officer who took part in the original decision, when someone tries to assign them, then the assignment is refused.</li><li>Given evidence that arrives after the reconsideration decision, when it is recorded, then it is left out of that decision's snapshot.</li><li>Given a ministry-requested extension without the required authorisation, when it is recorded, then the original time limit stands.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: the package from <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-058\">FR-058</a>. <em>Outputs</em>: the reconsideration <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#determination\">determination</a>. <em>Validations</em>: evidence is cut off at the moment of decision.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-061\">FR-061</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-058\">FR-058</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Policy requires both an independent reviewer and an evidence cut-off (OB-R02, OB-R08).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-058",
     "anchor": "fr-058",
     "title": "The appeal record is assembled from the decision record",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 7,
     "moduleText": "M7",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "The system builds the reconsideration package and the appeal record from the decision record, not by hand.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system builds the reconsideration package and the appeal record from the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#decision-record\">decision record</a>, not by hand. They contain the determination, the rules version, the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#watermark\">evidence snapshot</a> with where each fact came from, the trace, the notice exactly as issued and the client's submissions. The system severs them under <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#foippa\">FOIPPA</a> and supplies them to the tribunal and the client within the period the tribunal sets.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-002\">BR-002</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-003\">BR-003</a>, UC-4</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-R09, OB-R10, OB-A03, OB-A04</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n02\">N02</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n13\">N13</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given any determination, when the appeal record is requested, then it is built entirely from stored records, including the notice exactly as issued, byte for byte.</li><li>Given the assembled record, when it is released, then severing has been applied with a reason for each severed passage.</li><li>Given a first decision made by another body (for example <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#pbc-clbc\">Pacific Blue Cross</a>), when the ministry must reconsider it, then the administrator's record can be obtained under the terms of its contract.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: the decision record store. <em>Outputs</em>: the package and the severed appeal record. <em>Validations</em>: a completeness check against the record's inventory.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-078\">FR-078</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-008\">FR-008</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-009\">INT-009</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#replay\">Replay</a> lets the ministry reconstruct a decision for itself. Disclosure hands the record to the client so they can challenge it. A design that only supports replay fails the client (PRIN <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a> amendment (b)).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-059",
     "anchor": "fr-059",
     "title": "The tribunal is an outside party",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 7,
     "moduleText": "M7",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "The tribunal is an outside party listed in the integration inventory.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The tribunal is an outside party listed in the integration inventory. For each appeal the system records how the appeal ended (decided, withdrawn or abandoned) separately from the panel's decision (confirmed or rescinded). It takes in the panel's decision as a decision made by an outside body. It records evidence that entered at the hearing with the hearing as its source. It carries out a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#invalidation\">rescission</a> by cancelling the original decision and making a new one, never by editing it. It keeps the ministry's representative separate from the original decision-maker and the reconsideration officer.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-002\">BR-002</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-003\">BR-003</a>, UC-4</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-A05, OB-A06, OB-A07, OB-A09, OB-A14</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n02\">N02</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given an appeal outcome, when it is recorded, then only the panel decisions the statute allows are available, and a withdrawn or abandoned appeal has no panel decision <span class=\"cite\">NOTE6-C1</span>.</li><li>Given a rescission, when it is recorded, then the original determination is cancelled without being replaced, and a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#work-item\">work item</a> to make a new determination is created.</li><li>Given the choice of the ministry's representative at a hearing, when the candidate made or reconsidered the decision, then the assignment is refused.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: tribunal decisions (<a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-011\">INT-011</a>). <em>Outputs</em>: appeal outcomes and outside decisions. <em>Validations</em>: only the statutory terms are allowed.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-011\">INT-011</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-060\">FR-060</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>The panel can only confirm or rescind, and it may consider evidence that is not in the record. If the list of outcomes is wider than the statute allows, people will use the extra options (NOTE-006).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-060",
     "anchor": "fr-060",
     "title": "Putting a decision right, and undoing recovery",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 7,
     "moduleText": "M7",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "When a client wins, the system makes a new retroactive determination and calculates the difference from the old one.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>When a client wins, the system makes a new retroactive determination and calculates the difference from the old one. It then pays the underpayment or reverses the overpayment. Where an overpayment is reversed, the system automatically undoes any recovery already taken (deductions, <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#set-off\">set-offs</a>, collections referrals) and issues a corrected notice.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-003\">BR-003</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-005\">BR-005</a>, UC-4</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-A10</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n06\">N06</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given an allowed appeal that reverses an overpayment, when the new determination is issued, then recovery already taken is reversed and a corrected notice goes out with no manual step <span class=\"cite\">TA-C20</span>.</li><li>Given an underpayment to be put right, when it is calculated, then it is paid through the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#issuance-service\">chokepoint</a> with its purpose code.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: the outcome and the old and new determinations. <em>Outputs</em>: payments to put things right, and reversals. <em>Validations</em>: the amount is calculated, never typed in.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-052\">FR-052</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-042\">FR-042</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>A client who wins an appeal and still has money taken from their next payment is the most damaging fairness failure in this area (TA §C.8.4).</p>"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "h-statutory-time",
   "title": "H. Statutory time",
   "intro": "",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "FR-061",
     "anchor": "fr-061",
     "title": "One register of legal time limits",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 0,
     "moduleText": "M0 (register), M7",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "Every statutory and policy time limit is registered once as a clock with a unique identifier.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Every statutory and policy time limit is registered once as a clock with a unique identifier. Each clock records:</p><ul><li>its owner (the ministry, the client, the tribunal or an outside adjudicator);</li><li>its class (entitlement or service standard);</li><li>the event that starts it, how long it runs, and its <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#calendar-basis\">calendar base</a> and day type;</li><li>the extensions allowed and who must authorise each.</li></ul><p>The system detects and records a breach automatically. Where policy attaches a consequence, the system applies it without anyone asking. Business-day counting is one shared, tested capability.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-003\">BR-003</a>, UC-2, UC-4</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-R03, OB-R04, OB-R05, OB-R12, OB-A01, OB-A02, OB-A13</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#legal-time-limit\">clock register</a>, when it is loaded, then every clock states its owner, class, base and day type, with no defaults assumed. The obligation registers number clocks within each partition, and 18 of those numbers repeat across partitions; each clock gets a unique identifier instead.</li><li>Given a ministry-owned <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#clock-class\">entitlement clock</a>, when it is breached, then the breach is recorded and its effect on the effective date passes to <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-005\">FR-005</a> automatically.</li><li>Given a clock the ministry does not own, when it is breached, then the ministry bears no consequence for a breach it could not avoid.</li><li>Given day counting, when it is tested across holidays, year ends and February's shorter night counts, then every registered base counts correctly.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: the provincial holiday calendar (reference data) and the start events. <em>Outputs</em>: running clocks and breach events. <em>Validations</em>: each clock is versioned and effective-dated like a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#rules-engine\">rules artefact</a>.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-090\">FR-090</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-094\">FR-094</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Legal time limits are modelled once and used by every program <span class=\"cite\">TA-C21</span>. A missed deadline changes what the client is owed <span class=\"cite\">PRIN-C1</span>. Policy contains 138 clocks.</p>"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "i-notices-and-correspondence",
   "title": "I. Notices and correspondence",
   "intro": "",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "FR-062",
     "anchor": "fr-062",
     "title": "Notices are built from the decision record",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 2,
     "moduleText": "M2",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "Every notice that conveys a decision is produced from the determination record and a template version.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Every notice that conveys a decision is produced from the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#determination\">determination</a> record and a template version. The template version is fingerprinted and stored in that record as the fifth bound artefact, so the same inputs always produce the same notice. Content designers write templates against a registered list of variables. Templates are reviewed for plain language, for legal content where they convey a decision or a right, and for accessibility. They are then approved and released through the rules pipeline. Old templates are superseded, never deleted.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-002\">BR-002</a>, UC-1, UC-4</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n10\">N10</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a determination and its bound template version, when the notice is produced again years later, then it is identical, byte for byte, to the notice issued <span class=\"cite\">TA-C22</span>.</li><li>Given a template that uses an undeclared variable, when it is validated, then validation fails.</li><li>Given a notice that conveys a decision, when it is issued, then the finished document itself is kept.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#decision-record\">determination record</a> and the template version. <em>Outputs</em>: the finished notice and its delivery details. <em>Validations</em>: variables come from the record, never from live data.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-008\">FR-008</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-090\">FR-090</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>A tribunal asks what the client was told as often as what was decided (TA §C.8.6).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-063",
     "anchor": "fr-063",
     "title": "Rights wording and what every notice must say",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 2,
     "moduleText": "M2, M7",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Every notice of a decision, change or overpayment states what changed, why, when it takes effect, the legislation applied and the information used.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Every notice of a decision, change or overpayment states what changed, why, when it takes effect, the legislation applied and the information used. The system writes the rights section (whether and how to ask for reconsideration or appeal, and to whom) from the entitlement's <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#adjudicability\">adjudicability</a> attributes. The prescribed brochure and request form go with every adverse decision. The request form is included even where reconsideration is not available.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-003\">BR-003</a>, UC-1, UC-2, UC-4</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-D12, OB-R17, OB-EL-10, OB-EL-30, OB-EL-43, OB-EL-77, OB-IN-28, OB-IN-42, OB-SU-60</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n20\">N20</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given an entitlement that can be reconsidered but not appealed, when its adverse notice is produced, then it offers reconsideration and does not offer appeal.</li><li>Given an entitlement whose appeals go to an outside body, when its notice is produced, then it names that body.</li><li>Given any adverse notice, when it is issued, then the brochure and request form are in the package delivered.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: adjudicability attributes and the determination. <em>Outputs</em>: the rights section. <em>Validations</em>: nobody types rights wording by hand.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-062\">FR-062</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-092\">FR-092</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Getting adjudicability wrong hurts the client either way: offering a route that does not exist, or hiding one that does (PRIN <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n20\">N20</a>).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-064",
     "anchor": "fr-064",
     "title": "Delivery, proof of service and deemed receipt",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 2,
     "moduleText": "M2",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "The system tells apart a notice that was issued, delivered, deemed received and proven served.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system tells apart a notice that was issued, delivered, deemed received and proven served. It calculates <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#deemed-receipt\">deemed receipt</a> from the clock artefact. It records the date the client was told on the decision record, separately from the date of the decision. It uses deemed receipt to state, on the notice, how long the client has to respond.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-003\">BR-003</a>, UC-1, UC-4</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-D08</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a notice, when it states how long the client has to seek recourse, then the period comes from the deemed-receipt rule in the clock artefact, so the tribunal and the ministry always apply the same date <span class=\"cite\">TA-C23</span>.</li><li>Given a notice, when an operator tries to set the deemed-receipt date by hand, then there is no field to do it.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: delivery events (<a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-003\">INT-003</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-004\">INT-004</a>). <em>Outputs</em>: the notification date on the record. <em>Validations</em>: deemed receipt is calculated.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-061\">FR-061</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-003\">INT-003</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-004\">INT-004</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>The date the client is told starts their clock, and it differs from the date of the decision (OB-D08).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-065",
     "anchor": "fr-065",
     "title": "Languages, plain language and accessible formats",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 2,
     "moduleText": "M2",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Templates and reasons wording exist in every language the ministry must use for correspondence, and the system records the language each notice went out in.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Templates and reasons wording exist in every language the ministry must use for correspondence, and the system records the language each notice went out in. A translation is its own template version, approved separately. A published readability standard applies when templates are written. Accessible formats are available on request. The system stores a request as a client preference with an effective date and uses it by default.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-009\">BR-009</a>, UC-1</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n15\">N15</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a client's format preference, when any later notice of a decision goes out, then it uses that format without the client asking again.</li><li>Given a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#replay\">replayed</a> determination, when its notice is reproduced, then it is in the language that was actually sent.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: client preferences. <em>Outputs</em>: language and format on the notice record. <em>Validations</em>: a readability check when templates are written.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-062\">FR-062</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>A person cannot challenge reasons they cannot understand (TA §C.10.4). The ministry's language obligations and its plain-language standard are still to be confirmed, by the Chief Digital Officer with legal counsel.</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-066",
     "anchor": "fr-066",
     "title": "Interpretation and translation",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 3,
     "moduleText": "M3",
     "complexity": "Low",
     "lead": "The system helps staff arrange interpretation and translation through the contracted provider for applicants who need it.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system helps staff arrange interpretation and translation through the contracted provider for applicants who need it. It refuses documents needed to decide eligibility if they were translated by a source that cannot be checked, including search-engine or artificial-intelligence translation.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-009\">BR-009</a>, UC-1</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-IN-09, OB-IN-10</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n15\">N15</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n11\">N11</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a translated document submitted as evidence needed to decide eligibility, when its translation source cannot be checked, then it cannot be marked verified.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: interpretation requests. <em>Outputs</em>: interpretation records. <em>Validations</em>: the translation's source is recorded.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-073\">FR-073</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Policy bars AI from the evidence path for anything that decides eligibility <span class=\"cite\">OBLG-C8</span>.</p>"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "j-work-management",
   "title": "J. Work management",
   "intro": "",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "FR-067",
     "anchor": "fr-067",
     "title": "Work items, queues, and due dates from legal time limits",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 4,
     "moduleText": "M4",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "Work Management owns the task, and the case context owns the work.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Work Management owns the task, and the case context owns the work. <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#work-item\">Work items</a> have registered types and a typed link into the context that owns them. Assignment and reassignment are recorded as events with reasons. Queues use a pull or push discipline. Due dates come from legal time limits where one applies, and from service standards otherwise. Due dates set by a legal time limit are marked, and operations staff cannot change them.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-012\">BR-012</a>, UC-1, UC-4</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-EL-73, OB-IN-23</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n03\">N03</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a work item, when someone reassigns it without a reason, then the reassignment is refused.</li><li>Given a due date set by a legal time limit, when an operator tries to change it, then the change is refused <span class=\"cite\">TA-C24</span>.</li><li>Given a task record, when someone proposes adding a program-specific field to it, then design review rejects it because it rebuilds a shared model.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: work item types and clocks. <em>Outputs</em>: work items and their history. <em>Validations</em>: a typed link to the subject.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-061\">FR-061</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Named once, work management avoids five separate task models. Defined too broadly, it becomes the shared case model the architecture exists to prevent (TA §C.9.1).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-068",
     "anchor": "fr-068",
     "title": "Supervision, escalation and overdue work",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 4,
     "moduleText": "M4",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Overdue items show first on the worker's own view.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Overdue items show first on the worker's own view. Escalation adds a supervisor as a watcher once an item reaches a set age or state; it does not quietly reassign the item. A supervisor's view covers every team they own, across contexts.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-012\">BR-012</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given an item that meets its escalation rule, when it escalates, then it appears in the supervisor's queue and keeps its original assignment.</li><li>Given a supervisor, when they open their view, then items from every context their teams work in appear together.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: escalation rules. <em>Outputs</em>: supervisor views. <em>Validations</em>: escalation never reassigns.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-067\">FR-067</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Quiet reassignment destroys the record of who was accountable (TA §C.9.3).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-069",
     "anchor": "fr-069",
     "title": "Balancing caseloads, with a supervisor deciding",
     "priority": "Should",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 4,
     "moduleText": "M4",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "The system shows where caseloads are uneven and suggests how to redistribute them.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system shows where caseloads are uneven and suggests how to redistribute them. A supervisor decides, and the record shows the suggestion was advice only.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-012\">BR-012</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a suggested redistribution of ongoing casework, when it is applied, then a supervisor's decision is recorded and the suggestion is marked as advice.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: caseloads. <em>Outputs</em>: suggestions and decisions. <em>Validations</em>: ongoing casework is never reassigned automatically.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-067\">FR-067</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Moving an ongoing case changes the client's relationship with the ministry, so a person makes that call (TA §C.9.2).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-070",
     "anchor": "fr-070",
     "title": "Referrals to other bodies",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 4,
     "moduleText": "M4",
     "complexity": "Low",
     "lead": "The system records and routes the referrals the ministry must make:",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system records and routes the referrals the ministry must make: child protection concerns to the child protection authority, made by the staff member with direct knowledge; referrals for under-age applicants; and referrals to specialist ministry teams. It records the referral, who received it and the date.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-006\">BR-006</a>, UC-1</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-IN-17, OB-IN-18, OB-SU-76</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n02\">N02</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n13\">N13</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a child protection concern about a client or dependent child, when it is recorded, then a referral work item is created for the staff member with direct knowledge, and their report is documented on the case.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: evidence of the concern. <em>Outputs</em>: referral records. <em>Validations</em>: the recipient and legal basis are recorded.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-013\">INT-013</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-077\">FR-077</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>The duty to report falls on the individual and comes from statute (OB-IN-18; DRV-08).</p>"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "k-documents-capture-and-signature",
   "title": "K. Documents, capture and signature",
   "intro": "",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "FR-071",
     "anchor": "fr-071",
     "title": "Documents captured from every channel, with arrival date and context",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 3,
     "moduleText": "M3",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Documents come in by office scanning, client upload, photos from a phone, worker upload, mail and fax, and partner submission.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Documents come in by office scanning, client upload, photos from a phone, worker upload, mail and fax, and partner submission. Every route records the capture date, the arrival date where different, who captured it, the channel, and the request or case it answers. When a client uploads a document, the system tells them straight away if something is wrong with it.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-009\">BR-009</a>, UC-1, UC-2</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n15\">N15</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a document from any route, when it is stored, then its arrival date, channel, capturer and request reference are present. A document with no request context becomes an orphan <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#work-item\">work item</a>.</li><li>Given a paper document scanned later, when it is stored, then its arrival date is the day it physically arrived, and any clock runs from that date.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: documents. <em>Outputs</em>: document records. <em>Validations</em>: size, type, page count and format are checked at capture.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-072\">FR-072</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Documents with no link to a request cause most \"we never received it\" disputes, and a clock runs from the arrival date (TA §C.11.1).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-072",
     "anchor": "fr-072",
     "title": "Classification, inherited retention and malware scanning",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 3,
     "moduleText": "M3",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "A document attaches to evidence, to a case or to both, through a typed link.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>A document attaches to evidence, to a case or to both, through a typed link. It takes the stricter of its own classification and that of what it is attached to, and it keeps the retention of what it supports. Every incoming file is scanned for malware before anyone can reach it, and scanned again when the malware signatures are updated. Anything derived from a document (extracted text, search indexes, thumbnails) carries the document's classification and is disposed of with it.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-006\">BR-006</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-007\">BR-007</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n12\">N12</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n13\">N13</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a document disposed of with its subject, when <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#disposition\">disposition</a> runs, then extracted text, index entries, thumbnails and in-between copies are disposed of too, as the published list for documents requires.</li><li>Given a file caught by a later signature update, when the rescan runs, then it is quarantined and a work item is raised.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: classification at capture. <em>Outputs</em>: the scan result, kept as part of the document's state. <em>Validations</em>: each document is stored where its classification allows.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/data#dr-003\">DR-003</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/data#dr-004\">DR-004</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Document processing makes copies in more places than any other part of the platform (TA §C.11.2).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-073",
     "anchor": "fr-073",
     "title": "Values read by machine are unverified evidence",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 3,
     "moduleText": "M3",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Values produced by text recognition, classification or extraction come in as evidence.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Values produced by text recognition, classification or extraction come in as evidence. They record that a machine extracted them, the extractor's version, a confidence for each field and the part of the page they came from. They start as unverified. Extraction never marks a value verified, and an adverse <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#determination\">determination</a> cannot rest on an unverified extracted value.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-002\">BR-002</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-005\">BR-005</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n07\">N07</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given an extracted value, when it is stored, then its status is unverified and it points to the document, page and area <span class=\"cite\">TA-C25</span>.</li><li>Given an adverse outcome with any unverified extracted input, when it is calculated, then it is held for a person to decide (<a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-003\">FR-003</a>).</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: extractor output. <em>Outputs</em>: <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#fact\">evidence assertions</a>. <em>Validations</em>: only a person, or a check against an authoritative source, can verify a value.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-003\">FR-003</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>The comparator jurisdiction failed to separate \"the system read the document\" from \"the fact is true\" (TA §C.11.4).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-074",
     "anchor": "fr-074",
     "title": "Signatures and attestations",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 3,
     "moduleText": "M3",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "The system supports three kinds of signature:",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system supports three kinds of signature: attestation, a captured signature and a digital signature. Legal advice decides which kind each instrument needs. For every kind the system keeps the signed document and a binding record of the exact text shown, who signed, how they were identified, when, and from which session.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-002\">BR-002</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-009\">BR-009</a>, UC-1</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given any signed instrument, when it is retrieved, then the exact text shown at signing can be retrieved, with how the signer was identified and when.</li><li>Given a transaction completed with help, when the client attests, then both the helper's identity and the client's attestation are recorded.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: the instrument and the kind of signature assigned to it. <em>Outputs</em>: the signed document and binding record. <em>Validations</em>: the kind of signature per instrument comes from reference data.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-027\">FR-027</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>A signature record without the text that was shown proves nothing about what the person agreed to (TA §C.11.5). Legal counsel still has to decide which instruments need which kind.</p>"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "l-information-governance",
   "title": "L. Information governance",
   "intro": "",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "FR-075",
     "anchor": "fr-075",
     "title": "Consents with scope, time limit and withdrawal",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 1,
     "moduleText": "M1",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Every consent is recorded as an instrument with a status (granted, scoped, expired, withdrawn), a stated scope and period, and the legal authority it relies on.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Every consent is recorded as an instrument with a status (granted, scoped, expired, withdrawn), a stated scope and period, and the legal authority it relies on. This covers verbal and written consents, consent to taxpayer information, screening consents and consents to disclose. Staff share information only when a consent, power of attorney or other authorising document is on record.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-006\">BR-006</a>, UC-1, UC-8</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-IN-07</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n02\">N02</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n13\">N13</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n21\">N21</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given each consent instrument policy names, when it is registered, then its time limit and how to withdraw it are stated, or the gap is recorded for a ministry ruling.</li><li>Given a withdrawn consent, when any check or disclosure that depends on it is attempted, then it is refused.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: evidence of consent. <em>Outputs</em>: consent records. <em>Validations</em>: scope is checked at the time of use.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-085\">FR-085</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>The analysis found thirteen consent instruments, and twelve state no way to withdraw consent. That is a missing step in the design, not missing data (NOTE-003).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-076",
     "anchor": "fr-076",
     "title": "Collect only what is needed",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 0,
     "moduleText": "M0",
     "complexity": "Low",
     "lead": "The system collects only the information needed to decide eligibility or deliver the service.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system collects only the information needed to decide eligibility or deliver the service. Each evidence type is registered against its purpose, and the system rejects fields that have not been declared.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-006\">BR-006</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-IN-11</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n02\">N02</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n12\">N12</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a form or screen, when it asks for a field not registered against a purpose, then the schema check fails.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: the evidence type registry. <em>Outputs</em>: a purpose on each type. <em>Validations</em>: a purpose is required at registration.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/data#dr-001\">DR-001</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#foippa\">FOIPPA</a> limits collection to what is necessary (OB-IN-11; DRV-03).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-077",
     "anchor": "fr-077",
     "title": "Disclosure only with a recorded legal basis",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 1,
     "moduleText": "M1",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Every disclosure is authorised against a legal basis and, where one exists, an agreement in the registry.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Every disclosure is authorised against a legal basis and, where one exists, an agreement in the registry. The system first establishes who is asking and who the information is about. It records each disclosure with the recipient, legal basis, agreement, date and what was released. Where information is disclosed without consent because of compelling circumstances, the system triggers the notice to the client that policy requires. Disclosures required by statute (for child protection, maintenance enforcement, coroners and elected members' enquiries) are set up with their conditions.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-006\">BR-006</a>, UC-8</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-EL-05, OB-EL-56, OB-IN-19, OB-IN-20, OB-IN-33, OB-IN-34, OB-IN-37, OB-IN-38, OB-IN-40, OB-IN-41</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n13\">N13</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n21\">N21</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n06\">N06</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a disclosure request with no recorded legal basis, when it is assessed, then it is refused.</li><li>Given a statutory disclosure request that policy says must be in writing and cite its authority, when either is missing, then it is refused and recorded.</li><li>Given any disclosure, when it is complete, then its record is kept in the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#shred-survivor\">shred-survivor set</a>.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: requests and agreements. <em>Outputs</em>: disclosure records. <em>Validations</em>: the requester's identity is established first.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-085\">FR-085</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-080\">FR-080</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Most information exchange happens because a statute permits it, not because the client consented. The model therefore starts from legal basis and treats consent as one case of it (TA §C.3.3).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-078",
     "anchor": "fr-078",
     "title": "Severing within sentences",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 3,
     "moduleText": "M3, M7",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "Whenever a record is released, the system can sever anything that would identify another person, including an informant, down to individual phrases inside free text.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Whenever a record is released, the system can sever anything that would identify another person, including an informant, down to individual phrases inside free text. It records a reason for each severed passage. This works across every context's records.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-002\">BR-002</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-006\">BR-006</a>, UC-4, UC-8</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-R10, OB-IN-35</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n13\">N13</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a case note that names an informant, when it is released, then the identifying phrases are severed with reasons and the rest is released.</li><li>Given a severed release, when it is audited, then the original, the severed version and the reasons can all be retrieved.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: records for release. <em>Outputs</em>: the severed document and a reason for each passage. <em>Validations</em>: narrative is stored in a structure that allows severing.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-058\">FR-058</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Case notes cannot be stored as one opaque block, because severing at the point of disclosure is a core capability <span class=\"cite\">OBLG-C5</span>.</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-079",
     "anchor": "fr-079",
     "title": "Correction requests and annotations",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 1,
     "moduleText": "M1",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "A request to correct personal information is received once and acted on across every context that holds the information.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>A request to correct personal information is received once and acted on across every context that holds the information. Where the ministry decides not to correct it, an annotation saying a correction was requested but not made is attached, and it travels with the record and every copy.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-006\">BR-006</a>, UC-8</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-IN-36</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n06\">N06</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a refused correction, when any copy of the information is displayed or disclosed, then the annotation goes with it.</li><li>Given an accepted correction, when it is recorded at the source, then every context holding a copy is listed and must act.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: correction requests. <em>Outputs</em>: corrections or annotations. <em>Validations</em>: the list of copies is complete.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/data#dr-007\">DR-007</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>A refused correction is itself a recorded fact that must travel with the record. Policy states the right to correction but gives no way to carry a correction to parties who already received the information (OBLG §6).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-080",
     "anchor": "fr-080",
     "title": "Limits on use travel with the information",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 0,
     "moduleText": "M0",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "Sometimes the ministry may lawfully hold information but is barred from using it a certain way.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Sometimes the ministry may lawfully hold information but is barred from using it a certain way. The bar can cover a detail used in assessing eligibility, a type of content sent to a particular recipient, contact with a particular person, disclosure of a subject, or an act of communication. The system records the bar on the information itself, and the bar travels with every copy. The system enforces it at the point of use: a request must state its purpose, the system refuses by default, and each blocked use creates an event.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-006\">BR-006</a>, UC-8</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-IN-24</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n21\">N21</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n06\">N06</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n07\">N07</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a bar on a fact, when the fact is copied into another context, then the copy carries the bar (verified by test).</li><li>Given a read that does not state its purpose, when it is made, then it is refused.</li><li>Given a barred use, when someone attempts it, then it is refused and an event is recorded <span class=\"cite\">PRIN-C3</span>.</li><li>Given a detail a client volunteered that is barred from use in assessing eligibility, when a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#determination\">determination</a> is calculated, then that detail is left out of the calculation but still available for its permitted routing use.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: <code>barred_from</code> and <code>permitted_for</code> on facts. <em>Outputs</em>: enforcement events. <em>Validations</em>: each fact is held once, with a bar per use; facts are never duplicated to express a bar.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/data#dr-006\">DR-006</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>No other rule catches lawfully held information reaching a use it was barred from. A bar missing when information is captured is missing from every copy made before it was added (PRIN <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n21\">N21</a>, §V).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-081",
     "anchor": "fr-081",
     "title": "Access-to-information requests",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 3,
     "moduleText": "M3",
     "complexity": "Low",
     "lead": "A formal access request received anywhere is sent immediately to the access and privacy office, with the date it arrived.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>A formal access request received anywhere is sent immediately to the access and privacy office, with the date it arrived. That starts the statutory response clock. Responses are built from the record stores, with severing applied.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-006\">BR-006</a>, UC-8</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-IN-39</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a written access request received at an office or through a portal, when it is recorded, then the system notifies the access and privacy office and the response clock starts from the date it arrived.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: requests. <em>Outputs</em>: routed requests. <em>Validations</em>: the received date is required.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-078\">FR-078</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-061\">FR-061</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Today, entering a request in the case system does not notify the office (OB-IN-39). The new system must.</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-082",
     "anchor": "fr-082",
     "title": "Restricting how a client can be served",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 4,
     "moduleText": "M4",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Some clients have restrictions on how they deal with the ministry:",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Some clients have restrictions on how they deal with the ministry: third-party administration, a designated worker, or limits on a particular channel. Each restriction is one revocable entitlement. It records who authorised it, the reasons, when it must be reviewed, and a refusal the client can challenge. The system applies it on every channel.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-009\">BR-009</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-012\">BR-012</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-IN-31</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n15\">N15</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n19\">N19</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a restriction, when its annual review is due, then a review <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#work-item\">work item</a> is created.</li><li>Given a restriction, when a client tries a restricted channel, then the system routes them as the restriction states and records the attempt.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: restriction decisions. <em>Outputs</em>: channel entitlements. <em>Validations</em>: the authority is recorded.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-086\">FR-086</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Today one revocable entitlement is held in five places (NOTE-003: Channel Entitlement and Service Restriction).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-083",
     "anchor": "fr-083",
     "title": "Representatives acting on a client's behalf",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 1,
     "moduleText": "M1",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Representatives, advocates, third-party administrators and trusted third parties act for a client under a recorded authority.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Representatives, advocates, third-party administrators and trusted third parties act for a client under a recorded authority. The system records the identity of whoever acts as the source of everything they do. Ministry employees cannot act as a client's third-party representative.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-009\">BR-009</a>, UC-1</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-IN-47</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n15\">N15</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a transaction completed with help, when it is recorded, then the helper's identity and authority are recorded separately from the client's. No shared login exists.</li><li>Given a ministry employee, when someone proposes them as a client's representative, then the registration is refused.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: authority documents. <em>Outputs</em>: representation relationships. <em>Validations</em>: the authority is current when the person acts.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-075\">FR-075</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Acting for someone else needs its own record, not a shared login (TA §C.12.3).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-084",
     "anchor": "fr-084",
     "title": "Custodianship and Indigenous data governance",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 0,
     "moduleText": "M0 (schema), M9",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "Every evidence type records its custodian, governance regime, access conditions and transfer status.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Every evidence type records its <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#custodian\">custodian</a>, governance regime, access conditions and transfer status. The system works these out for each subject when someone asks for access, and the authorization policy applies them. Transferring records to another sovereign is one way a record can leave the system. It produces a defined transfer package, a defined set of records the ministry keeps, and a chained event recording the change of custodian.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-008\">BR-008</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n13\">N13</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n12\">N12</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given any evidence type and subject, when someone asks who the custodian is, then the system answers from a stored attribute, not from custom.</li><li>Given a transfer to another sovereign, when the package is produced, then the receiving body can check its integrity with the offline verifier, without using ministry systems.</li><li>Given a transfer date, when access is assessed after it, then the policy engine applies the new rules from <code>transfer_status</code> without anyone issuing an instruction.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: custodianship attributes. <em>Outputs</em>: transfer packages and change-of-custodian events. <em>Validations</em>: custodianship is worked out per subject.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/data#dr-005\">DR-005</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-085\">FR-085</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>A Nation's control over its own data cannot be expressed as a retention rule or an access list, and the attribute cannot be added later (TA §B.8).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-085",
     "anchor": "fr-085",
     "title": "The agreement registry is the only source of access rights",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 0,
     "moduleText": "M0/M1",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "Data-sharing agreements are stored as machine-readable records in a registry.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#sharing-agreement\">Data-sharing agreements</a> are stored as machine-readable records in a registry. Each records the parties, the services allowed, the authority relied on, the purpose, retention and onward-sharing terms, expiry and review dates, the accountable executives, its status and its history. All gateway and access settings are generated from the registry, and no access decision comes from anywhere else. The registry treats provincial public bodies, federal institutions, Indigenous governing bodies and contracted providers as separate kinds of party, each with its own vocabulary of legal basis.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-006\">BR-006</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-008\">BR-008</a>, UC-8</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n13\">N13</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n21\">N21</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n18\">N18</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given the gateway's administration interface, when any credential other than the generator's tries to create a route or consumer, then it is refused.</li><li>Given an Indigenous governing body, when an agreement is recorded, then it uses the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#non-crown\">non-Crown</a> party type and its own legal-basis vocabulary, not a provincial statutory head.</li><li>Given an agreement that reaches its review date, when the date passes, then an event is raised automatically.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: agreements. <em>Outputs</em>: generated settings. <em>Validations</em>: every access right traces back to an agreement.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-022\">INT-022</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/quality#nfr-sec-003\">NFR-SEC-003</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Once anyone grants access outside the registry, the link between legal authority and system access is broken and cannot be rebuilt (TA §C.3.4; decision D8).</p>"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "m-channels-reach-and-safety",
   "title": "M. Channels, reach and safety",
   "intro": "",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "FR-086",
     "anchor": "fr-086",
     "title": "Every channel reaches the same outcome, with help available",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": null,
     "moduleText": "every capture module",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Anything a client can do online they can also do by phone or in person, with the same effect as evidence and the same clocks.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Anything a client can do online they can also do by phone or in person, with the same effect as evidence and the same clocks. No statutory right, notice or recourse period is available only online. Where a client prefers paper, every notice of a decision goes out on paper by default. The contact centre's screens use the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#interface\">published contract</a> as fully as any other channel.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-009\">BR-009</a>, UC-1, UC-4</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n15\">N15</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given each journey in a context, when it is tested on every supported channel, then it completes and the outcome is the same on every channel <span class=\"cite\">TA-C8</span>.</li><li>Given the mix of channels, the volume of transactions completed with help, and whether outcomes match across channels, when each context gate is assessed, then all three are measured and reported.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: the channel register. <em>Outputs</em>: measures of whether outcomes match. <em>Validations</em>: every channel goes through the published contract.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-083\">FR-083</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-088\">FR-088</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>The clients least able to use a portal make up a large share of this caseload (TA §C.12.3).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-087",
     "anchor": "fr-087",
     "title": "Duty to accommodate",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 1,
     "moduleText": "M1",
     "complexity": "Low",
     "lead": "The system records a client's accommodation needs as lasting attributes:",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system records a client's accommodation needs as lasting attributes: communication barriers, interpreter needs, preferred names and designated-worker arrangements. It applies them on every channel. Staff make every reasonable effort to accommodate unless there is a clear and justifiable reason, which is recorded.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-009\">BR-009</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-IN-29</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n15\">N15</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a recorded accommodation, when the client contacts the ministry on any channel, then staff can see the accommodation and it is applied.</li><li>Given an accommodation that is not provided, when that is recorded, then the reason and the person who decided are recorded.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: accommodation requests. <em>Outputs</em>: accommodation attributes. <em>Validations</em>: each has an effective date.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-082\">FR-082</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>The <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#duty-accommodate\">duty to accommodate</a> comes from the <em>Human Rights Code</em> (OB-IN-29; DRV-05) <span class=\"cite\">BPCM-C2</span>.</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-088",
     "anchor": "fr-088",
     "title": "Online services for clients",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 1,
     "moduleText": "M1–M3 (reads, correspondence, capture), M8",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "Using the provincial digital identity, clients can apply, report changes, upload documents, receive and read notices, message the ministry, check status, ask for reconsideration and manage their preferences online.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Using the provincial digital identity, clients can apply, report changes, upload documents, receive and read notices, message the ministry, check status, ask for reconsideration and manage their preferences online. All of these use the same published contract as every other channel. Mobile uses the same service and has no separate back end.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-009\">BR-009</a>, UC-1, UC-2, UC-4</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n15\">N15</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n10\">N10</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given each client transaction, when it is done online, then it calls the same operation in the published contract as the route where a worker helps.</li><li>Given a client using a mobile browser, when they complete a transaction, then no separate mobile back end is involved.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: client transactions. <em>Outputs</em>: evidence and requests. <em>Validations</em>: the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#identity-assurance\">assurance level</a> of the client's login is recorded.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-005\">INT-005</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-086\">FR-086</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>A separate mobile back end would be a second channel with a second set of controls (TA §C.12.1).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-089",
     "anchor": "fr-089",
     "title": "Client and staff safety",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 1,
     "moduleText": "M1, M4",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "The system applies fleeing-abuse and safety flags to everyone on a case they concern.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system applies fleeing-abuse and safety flags to everyone on a case they concern. It blocks contact with an accused abuser, and any contact that would raise a safety concern. It records safety concerns about hearings and makes sure someone acts on them. It supports staff safety devices and procedures in offices.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-012\">BR-012</a>, UC-1, UC-4</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-A12, OB-IN-22</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n21\">N21</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n15\">N15</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n18\">N18</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a fleeing-abuse flag on a case, when any letter or contact would reach the accused person, then it is blocked and the attempt is recorded.</li><li>Given a safety concern about a hearing, when it is recorded, then a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#work-item\">work item</a> is created for the responsible action, with an owner.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: safety concerns. <em>Outputs</em>: flags and bars. <em>Validations</em>: the flag covers dependants as well as the applicant.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-080\">FR-080</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>A bar on contact with a particular person, and a bar on an act of communication, are limits on use in their own right (PRIN <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n21\">N21</a>). Staff safety is part of the nature of the work (DRV-10).</p>"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "n-rules-adjudicability-and-automated-decisions",
   "title": "N. Rules, adjudicability and automated decisions",
   "intro": "",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "FR-090",
     "anchor": "fr-090",
     "title": "Policy staff write rules as versioned, effective-dated artefacts",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 0,
     "moduleText": "M0 (minimum viable), M5",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "Eligibility rules, rates, clocks and reasons wording are versioned artefacts.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Eligibility rules, rates, clocks and reasons wording are versioned artefacts. Each carries its policy citation and effective date. An embeddable engine runs them inside the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#determination\">determination</a> service. Policy analysts write and simulate them. They are released through a pipeline with review, sign-off by two people and legal sign-off, and tested against a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#regression-corpus\">regression corpus</a> that does not depend on any one engine. A change that reduces the corpus's coverage fails the pipeline.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-010\">BR-010</a>, UC-7</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n04\">N04</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n07\">N07</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n18\">N18</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given two named policy analysts working without help, when they write, simulate and release one real rate change end to end in a test environment, then it succeeds, and the time taken and help needed are recorded <span class=\"cite\">TA-C9</span>.</li><li>Given a released artefact, when it is inspected, then it is fingerprinted and tagged, carries its policy citation and effective date, and has a regression result.</li><li>Given a rule whose only authority is a spreadsheet, when someone tries to release it, then release is blocked until a policy citation exists or the rule is recorded as unauthorised for the ministry to decide.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: policy text and rate tables. <em>Outputs</em>: <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#rules-engine\">rules artefacts</a>. <em>Validations</em>: a citation and effective date are required.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p>D3 decision; <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-091\">FR-091</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Running the engine inside the service against a snapshot passed to it is what makes <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#pure\">pure evaluation</a> achievable (commitment 2). The business case for the rules platform is that rate changes no longer wait for a software release. That case assumes analysts can write rules in the tool, and nobody has tested that yet.</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-091",
     "anchor": "fr-091",
     "title": "A rules register whose date conflicts block release",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 0,
     "moduleText": "M0",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Every rule is held in a register with its wording, policy citation, effective marker, start and end dates, authority status (confirmed, several dates, conflicting dates, no marker, unauthorised) and where it lives today.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Every rule is held in a register with its wording, policy citation, effective marker, start and end dates, authority status (confirmed, several dates, conflicting dates, no marker, unauthorised) and where it lives today. Historic rates are captured once when policy is ingested, not fetched again later. Effective dates are taken from the marker on each block of text, never from the page's footer.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-010\">BR-010</a>, UC-7</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n04\">N04</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a rule with conflicting effective dates, when someone tries to release it, then release is blocked until a ministry ruling is recorded <span class=\"cite\">RULES-C3</span>.</li><li>Given a policy page being ingested, when effective dates are captured, then they come from the block's marker and never from the page's \"last updated\" footer.</li><li>Given a practice rule with no policy authority, when it is found, then it is recorded as unauthorised and not released.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: policy pages, archived rate tables, and the spreadsheets that decide entitlement once they are obtained. <em>Outputs</em>: register rows. <em>Validations</em>: a citation is required.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-090\">FR-090</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Nine rules carry conflicting effective dates in policy, three of them on a single page. A determination made between the two dates cannot be <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#replay\">replayed</a> with a certain result (RULES §3).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-092",
     "anchor": "fr-092",
     "title": "A register of what can be challenged, for each entitlement and variant",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 0,
     "moduleText": "M0 (register), M7",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "For every entitlement and every variant, the system records the statutory basis, whether decisions can be reconsidered, whether they can be appealed, and to which body.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>For every entitlement and every <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#variant\">variant</a>, the system records the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#statutory-basis\">statutory basis</a>, whether decisions can be reconsidered, whether they can be appealed, and to which body. The values are effective-dated and never inherited from a parent entitlement. A client can always ask, whatever the values say.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-003\">BR-003</a>, UC-3, UC-4</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Obligations",
       "html": "<p>OB-R13</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n20\">N20</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given the register, when it is loaded, then every entitlement and variant has all four values, or is marked unresolved and cannot be used to produce notices.</li><li>Given a variant whose parent can be appealed, when the variant's own policy says otherwise or says nothing, then the variant has its own value or is marked unresolved. It never takes the parent's.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: the 95-row <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#adjudicability\">adjudicability</a> register (<code>ARC-001-ADJ-v0.1</code>). <em>Outputs</em>: attributes used by notices and routing. <em>Validations</em>: an unresolved value blocks notices.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-090\">FR-090</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>The four values vary independently. One supplement can be reconsidered but not appealed; one variant loses reconsideration while its parent keeps it. None can be worked out from the others <span class=\"cite\">PRIN-C2</span>. Fifteen register rows are still unresolved on at least one of the four values.</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-093",
     "anchor": "fr-093",
     "title": "A register of automated decisions, suspended automatically when challenged",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 5,
     "moduleText": "M5",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "The system keeps a published register of the classes of decision it makes automatically.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system keeps a published register of the classes of decision it makes automatically. Each entry records the program, the rules and version range, the classification and who approved it, whether human review is needed and which <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#statutory-dm\">statutory decision-maker</a> delegated it, the reasons template, the volume, and how often decisions are challenged and overturned. When a class hits its registered trigger, the system automatically sends every decision in it to a person for review.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-002\">BR-002</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-005\">BR-005</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n17\">N17</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n18\">N18</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a class without an approved reasons template, when a decision in it would be issued, then it cannot be issued.</li><li>Given a class whose rate of decisions overturned against the ministry exceeds its registered threshold in a cycle, when the cycle closes, then the class moves to human review, and decisions keep being issued with a person approving each one.</li><li>Given a class allowed to issue without human review, when its entry is read, then it cites the delegation from the statutory decision-maker <span class=\"cite\">TA-C2</span>.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: challenge and outcome data. <em>Outputs</em>: the register and suspension events. <em>Validations</em>: only the governance decision can reinstate a class.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-003\">FR-003</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>The comparator was missing a rule about which outputs count as decisions; more testing would not have caught it (TA §D.5).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-094",
     "anchor": "fr-094",
     "title": "Reference data with one owner and effective dates",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 0,
     "moduleText": "M0",
     "complexity": "Medium",
     "lead": "Reference data that drives decisions and controls has one master, effective dates, publication as events, and change control.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Reference data that drives decisions and controls has one master, effective dates, publication as events, and change control. It includes the provincial holiday calendar, the delegated authority schedule, value bands, approval and write-off thresholds, pre-flight thresholds, emergency ceilings and deemed-receipt rules.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-004\">BR-004</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-010\">BR-010</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n04\">N04</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n05\">N05</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n01\">N01</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a threshold a control uses, when it is changed, then the change is versioned with an effective date and an approver, and no deployment is needed.</li><li>Given any system that needs reference data, when it uses it, then it reads the published master and keeps no copy of its own.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: approved changes. <em>Outputs</em>: reference data events. <em>Validations</em>: the schema compatibility policy applies.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/quality#nfr-i-003\">NFR-I-003</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Each financial control threshold is a setting under change control, not a value fixed in a deployment (TA §C.6.5).</p>"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "o-transition-assurance-and-analytics",
   "title": "O. Transition assurance and analytics",
   "intro": "",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "FR-095",
     "anchor": "fr-095",
     "title": "Shadow comparison against recorded inputs",
     "priority": "Must",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 5,
     "moduleText": "M5",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "While old and new systems run side by side, each legacy determination records a snapshot of exactly what the legacy calculation read, from every legacy system that runs program logic.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>While old and new systems run side by side, each legacy <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#determination\">determination</a> records a snapshot of exactly what the legacy calculation read, from every <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#old-system\">legacy system</a> that runs program logic. The new determination service is then run against that snapshot. The comparison checks the structure of each result: the outcome, each rule, each input fact, the effective period and each component. Each difference is classified as a new-system defect, a legacy defect, a difference in policy interpretation, a data difference or rounding. Each class has its own exit criteria, which must hold for three monthly cycles in a row.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-001\">BR-001</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-011\">BR-011</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n07\">N07</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n05\">N05</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n18\">N18</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a comparison where two wrong components cancel out to the same total, when it runs, then it is reported as a difference <span class=\"cite\">TA-C26</span>.</li><li>Given a timing difference, when one is seen, then it is raised as a defect in the snapshot mechanism, not sent for adjudication.</li><li>Given a difference in policy interpretation, when it is found, then it goes to the standing panel's queue, and the panel's ruling is built into the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#rules-engine\">rules artefact</a>.</li><li>Given the legacy side of the comparison, when it is set up, then it includes every legacy place the calculation happens (including <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#old-system\">MIS</a> benefit calculation).</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: snapshots of legacy inputs and legacy <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#decision-record\">decision records</a>. <em>Outputs</em>: classified differences. <em>Validations</em>: difference records are classified and disposed of like any other client data.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-008\">FR-008</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-023\">INT-023</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/data#dr-014\">DR-014</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Comparing live against a lagging copy makes timing the main source of differences. Replaying against recorded inputs removes timing by design (TA §C.2.7). The legacy output is the benchmark to compare against, not the specification.</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-096",
     "anchor": "fr-096",
     "title": "Reports and analytics from the governed analytics platform",
     "priority": "Should",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": 1,
     "moduleText": "M1 onwards",
     "complexity": "High",
     "lead": "Operational, management and statutory reports come from the governed analytics platform without new copies of production data.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>Operational, management and statutory reports come from the governed <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#lakehouse\">analytics platform</a> without new copies of production data. So do the automated-decision register's rates, reconciliation and drift measures, and the decommission burn-down. Direct reporting from transactional databases is retired, or kept as a dated exception with a named owner.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-006\">BR-006</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-011\">BR-011</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n02\">N02</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n03\">N03</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n12\">N12</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a reporting user, when they get data, then it comes from the governed store at the level of detail they are entitled to, with no new extract.</li><li>Given a direct database read found on a transactional store, when it is found, then it is recorded in the channel register with a <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#disposition\">disposition</a> and an owner.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Inputs</em>: published events. <em>Outputs</em>: governed datasets. <em>Validations</em>: interactive queries must filter on a partition.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/data#dr-017\">DR-017</a>, D5</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>Downstream use must not need a copy (commitment 4). A conformed-dimension warehouse is already in production, so this is a migration, not a fresh start (APP §9).</p>"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "p-explicitly-excluded",
   "title": "P. Explicitly excluded",
   "intro": "",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "FR-097",
     "anchor": "fr-097",
     "title": "Card payment processing inside the ministry",
     "priority": "Won't",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": null,
     "moduleText": "n/a",
     "complexity": "Low",
     "lead": "The system does not process cardholder data.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system does not process cardholder data. Card payments go through the province's approved payment service, as one channel of the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#issuance-service\">Issuance Service</a>.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-004\">BR-004</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n11\">N11</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given any store, event or log, when it is scanned, then it contains no cardholder data <span class=\"cite\">TA-C27</span>.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Outputs</em>: tokens and settlement references only.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/integrations#int-025\">INT-025</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>The private cloud platform was never built to meet <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#pci\">PCI-DSS</a>. Processing cards in-house would be a programme in its own right (TA §C.6.7).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-098",
     "anchor": "fr-098",
     "title": "Automatic resolution of conflicting changes to client data",
     "priority": "Won't",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": null,
     "moduleText": "n/a",
     "complexity": "Low",
     "lead": "The system does not resolve conflicting changes to client data automatically.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system does not resolve conflicting changes to client data automatically. When the <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#old-system\">legacy system</a> changes a record the new system now owns, the change is rejected at source or sent to a person to reconcile within a service level. The latest change never simply wins.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-011\">BR-011</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n05\">N05</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given a legacy change to a record the new system owns for that group of clients, when it arrives, then it is rejected or queued for a person, never merged.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Outputs</em>: items in the reconciliation queue.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/data#dr-014\">DR-014</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>If software settles conflicts in data that decides what someone receives, a merge rule makes a choice that belongs to policy or to a person (PRIN <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n05\">N05</a>).</p>"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "FR-099",
     "anchor": "fr-099",
     "title": "Tribunal outcomes the statute does not allow",
     "priority": "Won't",
     "priorityNote": "",
     "module": null,
     "moduleText": "n/a",
     "complexity": "Low",
     "lead": "The system does not record \"allowed in part\" or \"referred back\" as panel outcomes.",
     "fields": [
      {
       "label": "Description",
       "html": "<p>The system does not record \"allowed in part\" or \"referred back\" as panel outcomes. The panel confirms or rescinds. Withdrawn and abandoned describe how an appeal ended, not what the panel decided.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Relates To",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/business#br-003\">BR-003</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Parameters",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n20\">N20</a>, <a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/parameters#n08\">N08</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Acceptance Criteria",
       "html": "<ul class=\"checks\"><li>Given the list of appeal outcomes, when it is inspected, then confirm and rescind are the only panel decisions.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Data",
       "html": "<p><em>Outputs</em>: statutory terms only.</p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Dependencies",
       "html": "<p><a class=\"rid\" href=\"%BASE%/requirements/functional#fr-059\">FR-059</a></p>"
      },
      {
       "label": "Rationale",
       "html": "<p>If the list of outcomes is wider than the statute allows, people will use the extra options. Two of the six values in the architecture's list have no <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#statutory-basis\">statutory basis</a> (NOTE-006). This exclusion amends <a class=\"g\" href=\"%BASE%/glossary#target-architecture\">target architecture</a> §C.8.2.</p>"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
};
